1
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:45,670
For more than a year, ominous rumors
Had been privately circulating...

2
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:48,173
among high-level Western leaders...

3
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:52,093
that the Soviet Union had been at work
on what was darkly hinted to be...

4
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:55,889
the ultimate weapon:
a doomsday device.

5
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:59,851
Intelligence sources traced the site
of the top-secret Russian project...

6
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:02,604
to the perpetually
fog-shrouded wasteland...

7
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:06,066
below the Arctic peaks
of the Zhokhov Islands.

8
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:11,488
What they were building or why it was
Located in a remote, desolate place...

9
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,823
no one could say.

10
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:45,558
General Ripper, sir.

11
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:47,560
Group Captain Mandrake speaking.

12
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,646
This is General Ripper speaking.

13
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,898
- Yes, sir.
- Do you recognize my voice?

14
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:54,401
I do, sir. Why do you ask?

15
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:56,236
Why do you think?

16
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:59,864
I don't know, sir. We spoke
just a few moments ago, didn't we?

17
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:05,203
You don't think I'd ask unless it was
pretty damned important, do you?

18
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:06,705
No, I don't.

19
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,957
Let's see if we can stay on the ball.

20
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:12,502
Has the Wing confirmed holding
at their fail-safe points?

21
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:15,422
Yes, sir. The confirmations
have just come in.

22
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:19,092
Very well.
Now, listen to me carefully.

23
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:21,970
The base is being put on condition red.

24
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:24,264
I want this flashed
to all sections immediately.

25
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,684
Condition red. Jolly good.
Keeps the men on their toes.

26
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:30,020
This is not an exercise.

27
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,939
Not an exercise?

28
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:39,279
I shouldn't tell you this, but you're
a good officer and have a right to know.

29
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,281
It looks like we're in a shooting war.

30
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:47,245
- Oh, hell. Are the Russians involved?
- That's all I've been told.

31
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:52,125
It came in on the red phone. I'm gonna
follow orders and seal this base tight.

32
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:56,755
Now, I want you to transmit Plan R...

33
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:58,757
R for Robert, to the Wing.

34
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:02,218
- Plan R for Robert.
- Is it that bad, sir?

35
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,763
- Looks like it's pretty hairy.
- Yes, sir.

36
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,890
Plan R for Robert.

37
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:10,310
Last and possibly most important...

38
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:14,606
I want all privately owned radios
to be immediately impounded.

39
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:18,610
They might be used to issue
instructions to saboteurs.

40
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:21,529
As I previously arranged, Air Police
will have lists of all owners.

41
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:25,617
I want every one collected
without exception.

42
00:05:25,658 --> 00:05:27,994
After you've done that,
report back to me.

43
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,774
In order to guard against
surprise nuclear attack...

44
00:05:57,857 --> 00:06:01,277
America's Strategic Air Command
maintains...

45
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:05,490
a large force ofB-52bombers
airborne24hoursa day.

46
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:10,453
Each B-52 can deliver
anuclearbombloadof50megatons...

47
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:15,542
equal to 16 times the total
explosive force of all the bombs...

48
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:20,171
and shells used by all the armies
in World War II.

49
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:23,383
Based in America,
the Airborne Alert Force...

50
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:26,261
is deployed from the Persian Gulf
to the Arctic Ocean.

51
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:29,139
But they have one geographical factor
in common.

52
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:33,184
They are all two hours
from their targets inside Russia.

53
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:56,184
Major Kong, I know you'll think
this is crazy...

54
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:59,938
but I just got a message from base
over the C.R.M. 114.

55
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:04,943
It decodes as Wing attack Plan R.
R for Romeo.

56
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:12,325
Goldie, did you say
Wing attack Plan R?

57
00:08:12,409 --> 00:08:13,952
Yes, sir, I have.

58
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:22,460
Goldie, how many times have
I told you guys that I don't want...

59
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,462
horsin' around on the airplane?

60
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,798
I'm not horsing around.
That's how it decodes.

61
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,509
I've been to one world fair,
a picnic...

62
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:33,471
and rodeo, and that's the stupidest
thing I heard over earphones.

63
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:35,432
You sure you got today's code?

64
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:37,976
Yes, sir.

65
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:40,603
There's gotta be something wrong.

66
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:43,023
Wait a second, I'm coming back.

67
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:21,186
Maybe you'd better get
a confirmation from base.

68
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,687
Yes, sir.

69
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:46,378
Major Kong, is it possible
this is some kind of loyalty test?

70
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:50,131
You know, give the go code and then
recall to see who would actually go?

71
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:54,344
Ain't nobody ever got
the go code yet.

72
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:56,805
Old Ripper wouldn't be giving us
Plan R...

73
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:59,516
unless them Ruskies had already
clobbered Washington...

74
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,893
and a lot of other towns
with a sneak attack.

75
00:10:01,935 --> 00:10:03,228
Yes, sir.

76
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,772
Major Kong,
message from base confirmed.

77
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,987
Well, boys, I reckon this is it.

78
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:17,325
Nuclear combat toe-to-toe
with the Ruskies.

79
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:37,262
Boys, I ain't much of a hand
at making speeches.

80
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:41,975
But I got a fair idea
that something doggone important...

81
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:44,060
is going on back there.

82
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:47,981
I've got a fair idea of the kind
of personal emotions...

83
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:51,526
that some of you fellows
maybe thinking.

84
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:54,320
Heck, I reckon you wouldn't be
human beings...

85
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:58,992
if you didn't have pretty strong
personal feelings about nuclear combat.

86
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:01,995
I want you to remember one thing.

87
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:04,831
The folks back home
are counting on you.

88
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:07,250
And by golly,
we ain't about to let them down.

89
00:11:08,585 --> 00:11:11,379
Tell you something else.

90
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:16,468
If this thing turns out to be half
as important as I figure it might be...

91
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:20,555
I'd say you're all in line
for some important promotions...

92
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:24,434
and personal citations
when this thing's over with.

93
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:27,270
That goes for every last one of you...

94
00:11:27,354 --> 00:11:31,191
regardless of your race,
color or your creed.

95
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,819
Now let's get this thing on the hump.
We got some flying to do.

96
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:50,669
Buck, should I get it?

97
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,671
Yeah, you'll have to.

98
00:11:58,593 --> 00:12:00,387
Hello?

99
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:05,016
Yes, General Turgidson is here,
but he can't come to the phone now.

100
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:07,394
This is his secretary, Miss Scott.

101
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,689
Freddie, how are you?

102
00:12:10,772 --> 00:12:13,066
Fine. And you?

103
00:12:13,108 --> 00:12:17,779
Oh, we were just catching up
on some of the general's paperwork.

104
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:22,492
He's tied up.
I'm afraid he can't come to the phone.

105
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:24,994
Just a minute.

106
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:28,331
General Turgidson,
a Colonel Puntrich calling.

107
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:30,333
Tell him to call back.

108
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:35,088
Freddie, the general says
could you call back in a minute?

109
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:37,090
He says it can't wait.

110
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:40,510
For Pete's--
Find out what he wants.

111
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:44,472
The general is in the powder room
right now.

112
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:46,808
Could you tell me what it's about?

113
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:52,355
Just a second. Apparently they monitored
a transmission eight minutes ago...

114
00:12:52,439 --> 00:12:54,899
from Burpelson Air Force Base.

115
00:12:56,776 --> 00:13:01,823
Right. It was directed to
the 843rd Bomb Wing on airborne alert.

116
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:07,078
It decoded as Wing attack Plan R.

117
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:12,792
Well, tell him to call what's-his-name,
Base Commander Ripper.

118
00:13:12,876 --> 00:13:14,544
Do I have to think of everything?

119
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:19,215
The general suggests you call General
Ripper, the 843rd base commander.

120
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:22,677
Oh. All communications are dead!

121
00:13:22,761 --> 00:13:26,139
Bull! Tell him to do it himself.

122
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:31,144
The general asks if you could
possibly try again yourself.

123
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:35,899
I see. He says he's tried personally
several times, but everything is dead.

124
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:38,735
Even the normal phone lines
are shut down.

125
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:48,828
Fred? Buck.
What's it look like?

126
00:13:50,455 --> 00:13:51,873
Yeah?

127
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:56,294
Well, are you sure
it's Plan R?

128
00:13:57,545 --> 00:14:00,256
Huh. What's cooking
on the threat board?

129
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,134
Nothing? Nothing at all?

130
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:07,347
I don't like the look of this.

131
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:11,476
Tell you what you better do,
old buddy.

132
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:14,688
You better give Elmo and Charlie a blast
and bump everything up to condition red.

133
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:17,315
Stand by the blower.
I'll get back to you.

134
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:19,609
- What's up?
- Nothing.

135
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:24,489
- Where's my shorts?
- On the floor. Where are you going?

136
00:14:24,531 --> 00:14:26,324
No place.

137
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:31,121
I thought I might mosey over to the
War Room to see what's doing over there.

138
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:32,997
It's 3:00 in the morning.

139
00:14:33,039 --> 00:14:35,000
The air force never sleeps.

140
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:39,004
Buck, honey, I'm not sleepy either.

141
00:14:41,673 --> 00:14:44,467
I know how it is, baby.

142
00:14:44,551 --> 00:14:46,553
Tell you what you do.

143
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:51,558
You start your countdown
and old Buck will be back...

144
00:14:51,641 --> 00:14:55,186
before you can say " Blastoff!."

145
00:14:56,479 --> 00:15:00,567
Your Commie has no regard
for human life, not even his own.

146
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:05,572
For this reason, men, I want
to impress upon you the need...

147
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,741
for extreme watchfullness.

148
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:11,870
The enemy may come individually
or he may come in strength.

149
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:14,539
He may even come in the uniform
of our own troops.

150
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:18,084
But however he comes,
We must stop him.

151
00:15:18,168 --> 00:15:20,920
We must not allow him
To gain entrance to this base.

152
00:15:22,464 --> 00:15:26,426
Now, I am going to give you
three simple rules.

153
00:15:26,468 --> 00:15:30,972
First: Trust no one,
Whatever his uniform or rank...

154
00:15:31,056 --> 00:15:33,558
unless he is known to you personally.

155
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,478
Secondly: Anyone or anything...

156
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:41,441
that approaches within 200 yards
of the perimeter is to be fired upon.

157
00:15:41,524 --> 00:15:47,155
Third: If in doubt, shoot first
and ask questions afterwards.

158
00:15:47,238 --> 00:15:50,617
I would sooner accept a few casualties
Through accident...

159
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:54,788
than lose the entire base
and its personnel through carelessness.

160
00:15:54,871 --> 00:15:59,000
Any variation on these rules
Must come from me personally.

161
00:16:00,085 --> 00:16:02,921
Now, men, in conclusion...

162
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:07,050
I would like to say
That in the two years...

163
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:10,929
that it has been my privilege
to be your commanding officer...

164
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:13,932
I have always expected
The best from you...

165
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:17,894
and you have never given me
anything less than that.

166
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:21,314
Today the nation is counting on us.

167
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:25,235
We are not going to let them down.

168
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,237
Good luck to you all.

169
00:16:57,434 --> 00:16:59,978
Here's the attack profile, sir.

170
00:17:27,714 --> 00:17:30,383
This is your attack profile.

171
00:17:30,467 --> 00:17:33,553
"To ensure that the enemy cannot monitor
voice transmission...

172
00:17:33,636 --> 00:17:35,805
or plant false transmission...

173
00:17:35,889 --> 00:17:41,019
the C.R.M. 114 is to be switched
into all receiver circuits.

174
00:17:41,061 --> 00:17:44,522
The emergency base code prefix
is to be set...

175
00:17:44,606 --> 00:17:47,025
on the dials of the C.R.M.

176
00:17:47,067 --> 00:17:51,654
This will block any transmission other
than those preceded by a code prefix. "

177
00:17:53,239 --> 00:17:55,367
Stand by to set code prefix.

178
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:57,911
Roger. Ready to set code prefix.

179
00:17:57,994 --> 00:17:59,871
"Set code prefix."

180
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:10,840
Code prefix set.

181
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:12,550
" Lock code prefix."

182
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:16,680
Code prefix locked.

183
00:18:16,763 --> 00:18:20,225
"Switch all receiver circuits
to C.R.M. discriminators."

184
00:18:21,434 --> 00:18:24,688
Switched to C.R.M. discriminators.

185
00:18:24,771 --> 00:18:26,606
"Check auto destruct circuits. "

186
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:31,861
Auto destruct circuits checked.

187
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:41,663
" Primary target:
the I.C.B.M. complex at Laputa.

188
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:45,959
Target reference:
Yankee, golf, tango...

189
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:48,086
3-6-0.

190
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:50,130
Thirty megaton nuclear device...

191
00:18:50,171 --> 00:18:54,259
fused for airburst at 10,000 feet.

192
00:18:54,342 --> 00:18:58,847
Twenty megaton nuclear device
will be used if first malfunctions.

193
00:18:58,930 --> 00:19:01,599
Otherwise, proceed to secondary target:

194
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:05,687
missile complex seven miles east
of Borchov.

195
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:09,733
Target reference:
November, bravo, Xray...

196
00:19:09,816 --> 00:19:12,277
1 -0-8.

197
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:17,657
Fused air burst at 1 0--"
Check-- " 1 2,000 feet."

198
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:32,839
Excuse me, sir. Something rather
interesting has just cropped up.

199
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:35,759
Listen to that. Music.
Civilian broadcasting.

200
00:19:37,344 --> 00:19:41,639
I think the Pentagon has given us
an exercise to check our readiness.

201
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:43,683
I think it's taking things too far.

202
00:19:43,767 --> 00:19:46,811
Our fellows will be inside Russian
radar cover in about 20 minutes.

203
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:50,106
Listen. Chock full of stations
all churning it out.

204
00:19:51,858 --> 00:19:53,651
- Mandrake?
- Yes, sir?

205
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:57,155
I issued instructions for all radios
to be impounded.

206
00:19:57,197 --> 00:20:01,534
You did, and I was in the process of
impounding this when I switched it on.

207
00:20:01,576 --> 00:20:05,080
I thought our fellows hitting Russian
radar, dropping all their stuff...

208
00:20:05,163 --> 00:20:09,626
I'd better tell you because if they do,
it'll cause a stink.

209
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:13,755
Group Captain,
the officer exchange program...

210
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:17,467
does not give you any special
prerogatives to question my orders.

211
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:21,763
I realize that, sir, but I thought
you'd be pleased to hear the news.

212
00:20:21,846 --> 00:20:24,599
After all, let's face it.

213
00:20:24,683 --> 00:20:28,687
We don't want to start a nuclear war
unless we have to, do we?

214
00:20:29,646 --> 00:20:33,316
Please sit down.
And turn that thing off.

215
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:34,526
Yes, sir.

216
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:39,489
What about the planes? Surely we must
issue the recall code immediately.

217
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:42,409
The planes are not going
to be recalled.

218
00:20:42,492 --> 00:20:45,370
My attack orders have been issued,
and the orders stand.

219
00:20:47,414 --> 00:20:51,543
If you'll excuse me for saying so,
that would be to my way of thinking...

220
00:20:51,626 --> 00:20:53,795
rather an odd way of looking at it

221
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:56,256
If a Russian attack was in progress...

222
00:20:56,339 --> 00:21:00,260
we would certainly not be hearing
civilian broadcasting.

223
00:21:00,343 --> 00:21:03,221
- Are you certain?
- I'm absolutely positive.

224
00:21:03,263 --> 00:21:06,016
What if it is true?

225
00:21:06,099 --> 00:21:09,102
I'm afraid I'm still not with you, sir,
because I mean...

226
00:21:10,687 --> 00:21:13,064
if a Russian attack
was not in progress...

227
00:21:13,106 --> 00:21:17,485
then your use of Plan R-- In fact,
your orders to the entire Wing--

228
00:21:24,951 --> 00:21:30,248
I would say, sir, that there was
something dreadfully wrong somewhere

229
00:21:31,291 --> 00:21:33,668
Why don't you take it easy,
Group Captain?

230
00:21:33,752 --> 00:21:36,421
Please make me a drink
of grain alcohol and rainwater...

231
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:38,923
and help yourself
to whatever you'd like.

232
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:52,062
General Ripper, sir, as an officer
in Her Majesty's Air Force...

233
00:21:52,145 --> 00:21:55,398
it is my clear duty
under the present circumstances...

234
00:21:55,482 --> 00:22:00,153
to issue the recall code upon my
own authority and bring back the Wing.

235
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:02,238
If you'll excuse me, sir.

236
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:15,752
Sir, I must ask you for the key and the
recall code. Have you got them handy?

237
00:22:15,835 --> 00:22:18,296
I told you to take it easy,
Group Captain.

238
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:20,965
There's nothing anybody can do now.

239
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:23,468
I'm the only person who knows
the three-letter code group.

240
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:26,096
I must insist
that you give them to me!

241
00:22:35,188 --> 00:22:39,150
Do I take it, sir, you are threatening
a brother officer with a gun?

242
00:22:40,443 --> 00:22:45,573
Mandrake, I suppose
it never occurred to you...

243
00:22:45,657 --> 00:22:49,244
that while we're chatting here
so enjoyably...

244
00:22:49,327 --> 00:22:53,206
a decision is being made
by the president...

245
00:22:53,248 --> 00:22:56,418
and the joint chiefs in the War Room
at the Pentagon.

246
00:22:57,502 --> 00:23:03,091
When they realize there is
no possibility of recalling the Wing...

247
00:23:03,174 --> 00:23:07,470
there will be only one course
of action open.

248
00:23:07,554 --> 00:23:09,431
Total commitment.

249
00:23:11,725 --> 00:23:16,146
Mandrake, do you recall what
Clemenceau once said about war?

250
00:23:17,439 --> 00:23:20,150
No, I don't think I do, sir. No.

251
00:23:21,818 --> 00:23:24,863
He said war was too important
to be left to the generals.

252
00:23:25,905 --> 00:23:30,535
When he said that 50 years ago...

253
00:23:30,577 --> 00:23:32,579
he might have been right.

254
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:34,998
But today...

255
00:23:35,081 --> 00:23:38,543
war is too important
to be left to politicians.

256
00:23:38,585 --> 00:23:43,048
They have neither the time,
the training...

257
00:23:43,131 --> 00:23:46,217
nor the inclination
for strategic thought.

258
00:23:49,846 --> 00:23:53,350
I can no longer sit back
and allow...

259
00:23:53,433 --> 00:23:58,563
Communist infiltration,
Communist indoctrination...

260
00:23:58,646 --> 00:24:00,273
Communist subversion...

261
00:24:01,775 --> 00:24:05,612
and the international
Communist conspiracy...

262
00:24:05,695 --> 00:24:08,573
to sap and impurify...

263
00:24:08,615 --> 00:24:11,951
all of our precious
bodily fluids.

264
00:24:18,124 --> 00:24:19,626
Staines, is everybody here?

265
00:24:19,709 --> 00:24:22,212
Mr. President, the secretary of state
is in Vietnam.

266
00:24:22,295 --> 00:24:26,257
The secretary of defense is in Laos, and
the vice president is in Mexico City.

267
00:24:26,299 --> 00:24:31,262
We can establish contact with them at
anytime. The undersecretaries are here.

268
00:24:31,346 --> 00:24:34,432
Right. General Turgidson,
what's going on?

269
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:38,561
Mr. President...

270
00:24:38,645 --> 00:24:42,273
about 35 minutes ago...

271
00:24:42,357 --> 00:24:46,361
General Jack Ripper,
the commanding general...

272
00:24:46,444 --> 00:24:48,863
of Burpelson Air Force Base...

273
00:24:48,947 --> 00:24:52,200
issued an order to the 34 B-52s
of his Wing...

274
00:24:52,283 --> 00:24:54,411
which were airborne at the time...

275
00:24:54,494 --> 00:24:58,623
as part of a special exercise we were
holding called Operation Dropkick.

276
00:24:58,665 --> 00:25:03,378
It appears that the order
called for the planes...

277
00:25:03,461 --> 00:25:06,840
to attack their targets
inside Russia.

278
00:25:06,881 --> 00:25:11,136
The planes are fully armed
with nuclear weapons...

279
00:25:11,177 --> 00:25:14,723
with an average load
of40 megatons each.

280
00:25:14,806 --> 00:25:19,269
The central display of Russia will
indicate the position of the planes.

281
00:25:20,729 --> 00:25:23,982
The triangles
are their primary targets.

282
00:25:24,024 --> 00:25:26,985
The squares
are their secondary targets.

283
00:25:28,028 --> 00:25:33,366
The aircraft will begin penetrating
Russian radar cover within 25 minutes.

284
00:25:35,535 --> 00:25:38,872
General Turgidson, I find this
very difficult to understand.

285
00:25:38,913 --> 00:25:44,210
I understood I was the only one
to order the use of nuclear weapons.

286
00:25:45,337 --> 00:25:49,424
That's right, sir. You are
the only person authorized to do so.

287
00:25:49,507 --> 00:25:53,803
And although I hate to judge
before all the facts are in...

288
00:25:53,887 --> 00:25:57,515
it's beginning to look like
General Ripper exceeded his authority.

289
00:25:57,557 --> 00:26:02,437
It certainly does, far beyond the point
I would have imagined possible.

290
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:06,149
Perhaps you're forgetting
the provisions of Plan R, sir.

291
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:08,068
Plan R?

292
00:26:09,444 --> 00:26:13,031
Plan R is an emergency war plan...

293
00:26:13,073 --> 00:26:15,617
in which a lower echelon commander
may order...

294
00:26:15,700 --> 00:26:18,828
nuclear retaliation
after a sneak attack...

295
00:26:18,912 --> 00:26:22,374
if the normal chain of command
has been disrupted.

296
00:26:22,457 --> 00:26:25,377
You approved it, sir.
You must remember.

297
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:30,757
Surely you must recall, sir,
when Senator Beaufort made...

298
00:26:30,799 --> 00:26:33,760
that big hassle about our deterrent
lacking credibility.

299
00:26:33,843 --> 00:26:38,598
The idea was for Plan R to be
a sort of retaliatory safeguard.

300
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:40,642
A safeguard?

301
00:26:40,725 --> 00:26:43,978
I admit the human element seems
to have failed us here.

302
00:26:44,062 --> 00:26:47,440
But the idea was to discourage
the Ruskies from any hope...

303
00:26:47,524 --> 00:26:52,112
they could knock out Washington, and
yourself, as part of a sneak attack...

304
00:26:52,195 --> 00:26:56,408
and escape retaliation because of lack
of proper command and control.

305
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:59,160
I assume the planes will return
automatically...

306
00:26:59,244 --> 00:27:01,246
once they reach their fail-safe points.

307
00:27:02,372 --> 00:27:06,918
I'm afraid not. The planes were holding
at their fail-safe points...

308
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:09,004
when the go code was issued.

309
00:27:09,087 --> 00:27:13,591
Once they fly beyond fail-safe, they do
not require a second order to proceed.

310
00:27:13,633 --> 00:27:15,593
They will continue
until they reach their target.

311
00:27:15,635 --> 00:27:18,722
Then why haven't you radioed the planes,
countermanding the go code?

312
00:27:20,390 --> 00:27:23,435
We're unable to communicate
with any of the aircraft.

313
00:27:23,476 --> 00:27:25,687
Why?

314
00:27:25,770 --> 00:27:28,148
As you may recall, sir...

315
00:27:28,231 --> 00:27:31,860
one of the provisions
of Plan R provides...

316
00:27:31,943 --> 00:27:36,531
that once the go code
is received...

317
00:27:36,614 --> 00:27:39,951
the normal S.S.B. radios
in the aircraft...

318
00:27:39,993 --> 00:27:42,495
are switched into
a special coded device...

319
00:27:42,537 --> 00:27:45,623
which I believe is designated
as C.R.M. 114.

320
00:27:45,665 --> 00:27:50,128
In order to prevent the enemy
from issuing fake or confusing orders...

321
00:27:50,170 --> 00:27:54,132
C.R.M. 114 is designed
not to receive at all...

322
00:27:54,174 --> 00:27:59,721
unless the message is proceeded by the
correct three-letter code group prefix.

323
00:27:59,804 --> 00:28:05,185
You mean to tell me you will be unable
to recall the aircraft?

324
00:28:05,226 --> 00:28:08,188
That's the size of it.
However, we are plowing through...

325
00:28:08,229 --> 00:28:11,149
every possible three-letter combination
of the code.

326
00:28:11,191 --> 00:28:16,404
But since there are
1 7,000 permutations...

327
00:28:16,488 --> 00:28:20,075
it's going to take us about two
and a half days to transmit them all.

328
00:28:20,158 --> 00:28:22,911
How soon will the planes penetrate
Russian radar cover?

329
00:28:22,994 --> 00:28:26,498
-About 1 8 minutes from now.
-Are you in contact with General Ripper?

330
00:28:26,539 --> 00:28:31,461
No, sir. General Ripper sealed off
the base and cut off communications.

331
00:28:31,544 --> 00:28:33,171
Where did you get this information?

332
00:28:33,213 --> 00:28:36,841
General Ripper called
Strategic Air Command Headquarters...

333
00:28:36,883 --> 00:28:39,427
shortly after he issued the go code.

334
00:28:39,511 --> 00:28:43,139
I have a portion of the conversation
transcript if you'd like me to read it.

335
00:28:43,223 --> 00:28:44,974
Read it.

336
00:28:46,768 --> 00:28:49,562
The duty officer asked
General Ripper...

337
00:28:49,604 --> 00:28:52,899
to confirm the fact that he had
issued the go code and he said:

338
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:58,196
"Yes, gentlemen, they are on their way
in and no one can bring them back.

339
00:28:58,238 --> 00:29:01,074
For the sake of our country
and our way of life...

340
00:29:01,116 --> 00:29:03,827
I suggest you get the rest of SAC
in after them.

341
00:29:03,910 --> 00:29:08,790
Otherwise, we will be totally destroyed
by Red retaliation.

342
00:29:08,873 --> 00:29:14,170
My boys will give you the best kind
of start: 1 ,400 megatons worth.

343
00:29:14,254 --> 00:29:17,799
And you sure as hell
won't stop them now.

344
00:29:17,882 --> 00:29:20,760
So let's get going.
There's no other choice.

345
00:29:20,802 --> 00:29:25,682
God willing, we will prevail
in peace and freedom from fear...

346
00:29:25,765 --> 00:29:29,144
and in true health
through the purity...

347
00:29:29,227 --> 00:29:33,106
and essence of our natural...

348
00:29:33,148 --> 00:29:34,607
fluids.

349
00:29:35,608 --> 00:29:37,569
God bless you all."

350
00:29:39,529 --> 00:29:42,157
Then he hung up.

351
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:45,827
We're still trying to figure out
the meaning of that last phrase, sir.

352
00:29:45,910 --> 00:29:50,248
There's nothing to figure out.
This man is obviously a psychotic.

353
00:29:50,290 --> 00:29:55,420
I'd like to hold off judgment
until all the facts are in.

354
00:29:55,462 --> 00:30:00,091
General Turgidson, when you instituted
the human reliability tests...

355
00:30:00,133 --> 00:30:04,095
you assured me there was no possibility
of such a thing ever occurring.

356
00:30:06,056 --> 00:30:10,101
Well, I don't think it's fair
to condemn a whole program...

357
00:30:10,185 --> 00:30:12,854
because of a single slip-up, sir.

358
00:30:12,937 --> 00:30:15,440
I want to speak to General Ripper
on the telephone.

359
00:30:15,523 --> 00:30:17,067
That's impossible.

360
00:30:17,150 --> 00:30:21,029
General Turgidson, I am becoming
less and less interested...

361
00:30:21,112 --> 00:30:24,657
in your estimates
of what is possible and impossible.

362
00:30:25,825 --> 00:30:27,285
General Faceman.

363
00:30:27,327 --> 00:30:28,495
Yes, sir?

364
00:30:28,578 --> 00:30:30,955
Are there any army units
stationed near Burpelson?

365
00:30:30,997 --> 00:30:33,083
I'll just check, sir.

366
00:30:37,921 --> 00:30:39,339
Hello?

367
00:30:40,924 --> 00:30:44,177
I told you never to call me here.
Don't you know where I am?

368
00:30:46,554 --> 00:30:49,224
Look, baby, I can't talk to you now.

369
00:30:49,307 --> 00:30:51,851
My president needs me.

370
00:30:51,935 --> 00:30:55,563
Of course Bucky would rather
be there with you.

371
00:30:56,648 --> 00:30:59,818
Of course it isn't only physical.

372
00:30:59,859 --> 00:31:02,362
I deeply respect you
as a human being.

373
00:31:02,404 --> 00:31:05,490
Someday I'm going to make you
Mrs. Buck Turgidson.

374
00:31:06,700 --> 00:31:09,619
Oh, listen, you go back to sleep.

375
00:31:09,703 --> 00:31:12,664
Buck will be there as soon as he can.

376
00:31:12,706 --> 00:31:17,335
All right. Listen, don't forget
to say your prayers.

377
00:31:24,342 --> 00:31:28,263
Apparently,
the 23rd Airborne Division...

378
00:31:28,346 --> 00:31:31,182
is stationed seven miles away
at Alvarado.

379
00:31:31,224 --> 00:31:35,520
General Faceman, I want them to enter
the base, locate General Ripper...

380
00:31:35,562 --> 00:31:37,939
and put him in immediate
telephone contact with me.

381
00:31:38,023 --> 00:31:39,649
Yes, sir.

382
00:31:39,733 --> 00:31:41,359
Mr. President?

383
00:31:41,443 --> 00:31:43,028
If I may advise.

384
00:31:43,111 --> 00:31:47,407
Under a condition red, it is standard
procedure that the base be sealed off...

385
00:31:47,449 --> 00:31:50,243
and the base defended
by base security troops.

386
00:31:50,285 --> 00:31:54,748
Any force trying to enter would
certainly encounter heavy casualties.

387
00:31:54,789 --> 00:31:58,877
General Turgidson, with all due respect
for your defense team...

388
00:31:58,918 --> 00:32:01,671
my boys can brush them aside
without too much trouble.

389
00:32:02,589 --> 00:32:07,385
Mr. President, there are one or two
points I'd like to make, if I may?

390
00:32:08,428 --> 00:32:09,846
Go ahead, General.

391
00:32:11,348 --> 00:32:16,019
One: Our hopes for recalling
the 843rd Bomb Wing...

392
00:32:16,102 --> 00:32:20,398
are quickly being reduced
to a very low order of probability.

393
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:23,485
Two: In less than 15 minutes
from now...

394
00:32:23,568 --> 00:32:26,571
the Ruskies will be making
radar contact with the planes.

395
00:32:26,613 --> 00:32:28,615
Three: When they do...

396
00:32:28,698 --> 00:32:32,327
they will go absolutely ape and
strike back with everything they've got.

397
00:32:32,410 --> 00:32:36,289
Four: If prior to this time...

398
00:32:36,373 --> 00:32:39,834
we have done nothing to suppress
their retaliatory capabilities...

399
00:32:39,918 --> 00:32:43,588
we will suffer virtual annihilation.

400
00:32:46,633 --> 00:32:51,304
Five: lf, on the other hand...

401
00:32:53,181 --> 00:32:58,520
we immediately launched an attack
on their airfields and missile bases...

402
00:32:58,603 --> 00:33:01,773
we'd stand a damn good chance
of catching them with their pants down.

403
00:33:01,856 --> 00:33:04,234
Hell, we've got
a five-to-one missile superiority.

404
00:33:04,317 --> 00:33:07,070
We could easily assign three missiles
to every target...

405
00:33:07,153 --> 00:33:10,532
and still have a very effective reserve
force for any other contingency.

406
00:33:10,615 --> 00:33:15,995
Six: An unofficial study which
we undertook of this eventuality...

407
00:33:16,037 --> 00:33:21,001
indicated that we would destroy
90% of their nuclear capabilities.

408
00:33:21,042 --> 00:33:23,169
We would therefore prevail...

409
00:33:23,253 --> 00:33:26,464
and suffer only modest and acceptable
civilian casualties...

410
00:33:26,506 --> 00:33:30,969
from their remaining force which would
be badly damaged and uncoordinated.

411
00:33:31,011 --> 00:33:34,472
General, it is the avowed policy
of our country...

412
00:33:34,556 --> 00:33:36,725
never to strike first
with nuclear weapons.

413
00:33:36,808 --> 00:33:41,479
Well, Mr. President, General Ripper
has already invalidated that policy.

414
00:33:41,563 --> 00:33:46,026
That was not an act of national policy.
There are still alternatives open to us.

415
00:33:47,027 --> 00:33:51,865
Mr. President, we are rapidly
approaching a moment of truth...

416
00:33:51,906 --> 00:33:55,076
both for ourselves as human beings
and for the life of our nation.

417
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:57,787
Truth is not always a pleasant thing.

418
00:33:57,871 --> 00:34:00,415
But it is necessary now
to make a choice:

419
00:34:00,498 --> 00:34:03,251
to choose between two admittedly
regrettable...

420
00:34:03,335 --> 00:34:06,796
but nevertheless distinguishable
postwar environments.

421
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:11,676
One, where 20 million people are killed;
the other, 1 50 people killed.

422
00:34:11,718 --> 00:34:14,721
You're talking about mass murder,
General, not war.

423
00:34:14,763 --> 00:34:18,350
Mr. President, I'm not saying
we wouldn't get our hair mussed.

424
00:34:18,433 --> 00:34:23,063
But I do say no more than
1 0 to 20 million killed. Tops!

425
00:34:23,146 --> 00:34:25,148
Depending on the breaks.

426
00:34:25,231 --> 00:34:29,194
I will not go down in history as
the greatest mass murderer since Hitler!

427
00:34:29,277 --> 00:34:31,863
It might be better
if you were more concerned...

428
00:34:31,946 --> 00:34:35,283
with the American people than
with your image in the history books.

429
00:34:35,367 --> 00:34:38,370
General Turgidson,
I've heard quite sufficient from you.

430
00:34:38,453 --> 00:34:40,872
Thank you very much.

431
00:34:40,914 --> 00:34:43,500
Mr. President, they have
the ambassador waiting upstairs.

432
00:34:43,583 --> 00:34:47,212
- Good. Any difficulty?
- He's having a fit about the M.P.s.

433
00:34:47,253 --> 00:34:49,756
That can't be helped.
Have him brought here straightaway.

434
00:34:49,798 --> 00:34:51,383
Yes, sir.

435
00:34:51,424 --> 00:34:53,968
Is that the Russian ambassador?

436
00:34:54,052 --> 00:34:56,137
Yes, it is, General.

437
00:34:58,264 --> 00:35:01,226
Am I to understand
the Russian ambassador...

438
00:35:01,267 --> 00:35:03,645
is to be admitted entrance
to the War Room?

439
00:35:03,728 --> 00:35:06,606
That is correct.
He is here on my orders.

440
00:35:09,484 --> 00:35:11,695
I don't know exactly how
to put this, sir...

441
00:35:11,778 --> 00:35:15,198
but are you aware of what a breach
of security that would be?

442
00:35:15,281 --> 00:35:19,411
He'll see everything.
He'll see the big board.

443
00:35:20,370 --> 00:35:22,706
That is precisely the idea, General.

444
00:35:22,789 --> 00:35:25,000
That is precisely the idea.

445
00:35:26,543 --> 00:35:30,463
Staines, get Premier Kissoff
on the hot line.

446
00:35:37,595 --> 00:35:41,474
"Survival kit contents check.

447
00:35:41,558 --> 00:35:46,479
In them you will find
one.45caliberautomatic...

448
00:35:46,563 --> 00:35:49,065
two boxes of ammunition...

449
00:35:49,149 --> 00:35:52,402
four days concentrated
emergency rations...

450
00:35:52,485 --> 00:35:55,822
one drug issue
containing antibiotics...

451
00:35:55,864 --> 00:36:00,201
morphine, vitamin pills,
pep pills...

452
00:36:00,285 --> 00:36:04,080
sleeping pills,
tranquilizer pills...

453
00:36:04,164 --> 00:36:09,002
one miniature combination
Russian phrasebook and Bible...

454
00:36:09,044 --> 00:36:12,088
$100 in rubles...

455
00:36:12,172 --> 00:36:14,299
$100ingold...

456
00:36:14,341 --> 00:36:17,135
nine packs of chewing gum...

457
00:36:17,177 --> 00:36:19,137
one issue of prophylactics...

458
00:36:19,179 --> 00:36:23,224
three lipsticks,
three pair of nylon stockings."

459
00:36:23,308 --> 00:36:28,021
Shoot, a fellow could have a pretty
good weekend in Vegas with that stuff.

460
00:36:33,526 --> 00:36:36,404
- You don't have any fresh fish?
- I'm afraid not, sir.

461
00:36:36,488 --> 00:36:38,656
- Your eggs are fresh?
- Yes, sir.

462
00:36:38,740 --> 00:36:42,702
I will have poached eggs. And bring me
some cigars, please. Havana cigars.

463
00:36:42,786 --> 00:36:46,206
That will be all, sir?
I'll see to it right away.

464
00:36:46,247 --> 00:36:49,459
Try one of these Jamaican cigars,
Ambassador. They're good.

465
00:36:49,542 --> 00:36:53,004
Thank you, no. I do not support the work
of imperialist stooges.

466
00:36:53,046 --> 00:36:55,674
Oh, only Commie stooges, huh?

467
00:36:55,715 --> 00:36:57,300
Mr. President.

468
00:36:59,177 --> 00:37:02,472
You're gonna let that lousy Commie punk
vomit all over us like this?

469
00:37:02,555 --> 00:37:03,640
Mr. President?

470
00:37:03,723 --> 00:37:07,477
They haven't reached Premier Kissoff.
They don't know where he is...

471
00:37:07,560 --> 00:37:09,938
and he won't be back for two hours.

472
00:37:11,022 --> 00:37:13,525
Try B-8-6-5-4-3 Moscow.

473
00:37:13,566 --> 00:37:15,694
You would never have found him
through his office.

474
00:37:15,735 --> 00:37:19,781
Our premier is a man of the people,
but he is also a man, if you follow.

475
00:37:19,864 --> 00:37:22,534
- Degenerate atheistic Commie.
- What did you say?

476
00:37:22,617 --> 00:37:26,204
I said Premier Kissoff is
a degenerate atheistic Commie!

477
00:37:26,246 --> 00:37:29,207
- Have this ignorant fool--
- I'm sorry!

478
00:37:29,249 --> 00:37:33,211
Mr. President,
I think they're trying the number.

479
00:37:43,847 --> 00:37:46,975
Gentlemen, you can't fight in here.
This is the War Room!

480
00:37:47,058 --> 00:37:49,894
What is going on here?
I demand an explanation.

481
00:37:49,936 --> 00:37:54,232
This clumsy fool tried to plant
that ridiculous camera on me.

482
00:37:54,274 --> 00:37:56,901
You bet your sweets, Mr. Commie!
Look at this, Mr. President.

483
00:37:56,943 --> 00:38:00,572
This lousy Commie rat was taking
pictures with this of the big board!

484
00:38:01,614 --> 00:38:03,491
Mr. Ambassador!

485
00:38:03,575 --> 00:38:07,829
This clumsy fool attempted to plant
that ridiculous camera on me.

486
00:38:07,912 --> 00:38:10,790
That's a damn lie!
I saw him with my own eyes.

487
00:38:10,832 --> 00:38:15,045
This is outrageous. I have never heard
of such behavior in the War Room before.

488
00:38:15,128 --> 00:38:17,589
Mr. President, I think
they're getting him on the line.

489
00:38:45,617 --> 00:38:47,535
You got to hand it to those Commies.

490
00:38:47,619 --> 00:38:52,123
Yeah. Those trucks sure look like
the real thing, don't they?

491
00:38:52,207 --> 00:38:54,167
I wonder where they got them from.

492
00:38:54,209 --> 00:38:56,503
Probably bought them
from the army as war surplus.

493
00:39:00,173 --> 00:39:04,260
Okay, open up at 200 yards.

494
00:40:01,484 --> 00:40:05,155
Tell him where you are and that
you'll speak if I say anything untrue...

495
00:40:05,238 --> 00:40:07,532
but nothing more than that.

496
00:40:09,117 --> 00:40:12,537
Alexi? Alexi, please.
I beg you.

497
00:40:13,580 --> 00:40:16,207
But I don't have a phone.

498
00:40:16,249 --> 00:40:18,835
Give him the phone.

499
00:40:45,612 --> 00:40:49,991
I've done as you asked.
Be careful. I think he is drunk.

500
00:40:52,994 --> 00:40:57,457
Hello? Hello, Dimitri?

501
00:40:57,540 --> 00:40:59,959
Listen, I can't hear too well.

502
00:41:00,001 --> 00:41:03,296
Could you turn the music down
a little?

503
00:41:03,338 --> 00:41:05,298
That's much better.

504
00:41:05,340 --> 00:41:07,967
Yeah. Yeah.

505
00:41:09,260 --> 00:41:12,055
Fine. I can hear you now, Dimitri.

506
00:41:12,138 --> 00:41:15,600
Clear and plain
and coming through fine.

507
00:41:15,684 --> 00:41:20,105
I'm coming through fine, too, eh?
Good.

508
00:41:20,146 --> 00:41:24,109
Well, then, as you say,
we're both coming through fine. Good.

509
00:41:24,192 --> 00:41:26,152
It's good that you're fine...

510
00:41:26,194 --> 00:41:28,488
and I'm fine.

511
00:41:28,530 --> 00:41:31,783
I agree with you.
It's great to be fine.

512
00:41:32,659 --> 00:41:34,869
Now, Dimitri...

513
00:41:34,953 --> 00:41:40,625
you know how we've always talked
about the possibility...

514
00:41:40,709 --> 00:41:43,420
of something going wrong
with the bomb.

515
00:41:44,796 --> 00:41:46,756
The bomb, Dimitri.

516
00:41:47,966 --> 00:41:50,593
The hydrogen bomb.

517
00:41:50,677 --> 00:41:53,638
Well, now, what happened is...

518
00:41:53,680 --> 00:41:57,934
one of our base commanders,
he had a sort of--

519
00:41:58,018 --> 00:42:01,229
Well, he went a little funny
in the head.

520
00:42:01,312 --> 00:42:04,399
You know, just a little funny.

521
00:42:04,482 --> 00:42:08,111
And he went and did a silly thing.

522
00:42:09,195 --> 00:42:11,114
I'll tell you what he did.

523
00:42:11,197 --> 00:42:13,533
He ordered his planes...

524
00:42:15,201 --> 00:42:17,662
to attack your country.

525
00:42:17,704 --> 00:42:20,123
Let me finish, Dimitri.

526
00:42:21,124 --> 00:42:23,084
Let me finish, Dimitri.

527
00:42:23,168 --> 00:42:26,338
Listen, how do you think
I feel about it?

528
00:42:26,421 --> 00:42:29,299
Can you imagine how I feel
about it, Dimitri?

529
00:42:30,842 --> 00:42:33,011
Why do you think I'm calling you?

530
00:42:33,053 --> 00:42:35,096
Just to say hello?

531
00:42:36,181 --> 00:42:38,558
Of course I like to speak to you!

532
00:42:38,641 --> 00:42:41,186
Of course I like to say hello!

533
00:42:41,227 --> 00:42:43,438
Not now, but anytime, Dimitri.

534
00:42:43,521 --> 00:42:47,525
I'm just calling up to tell you
something terrible has happened.

535
00:42:47,609 --> 00:42:50,612
Of course, it's a friendly call.

536
00:42:50,695 --> 00:42:54,949
Listen, if it wasn't friendly,
you probably wouldn't have even got it.

537
00:42:57,243 --> 00:43:02,040
They will not reach their targets
for at least another hour.

538
00:43:02,082 --> 00:43:05,210
I am positive, Dimitri.

539
00:43:05,251 --> 00:43:07,712
I've been all over this
with your ambassador.

540
00:43:07,754 --> 00:43:10,256
It is not a trick.

541
00:43:10,340 --> 00:43:11,800
I'll tell you.

542
00:43:11,883 --> 00:43:15,720
We'd like to give your Air Staff
a complete rundown on the targets...

543
00:43:15,762 --> 00:43:19,057
the flight plans
and defensive systems of the planes.

544
00:43:19,099 --> 00:43:24,062
Yes, if we're unable
to recall the planes...

545
00:43:24,104 --> 00:43:26,773
I'd say, well...

546
00:43:28,191 --> 00:43:32,570
we're just gonna have to help you
destroy them, Dimitri.

547
00:43:32,612 --> 00:43:35,573
I know they're our boys.

548
00:43:35,615 --> 00:43:38,159
Listen. Now, who should we call?

549
00:43:39,994 --> 00:43:44,499
Who should we call?
Sorry, you faded away.

550
00:43:45,709 --> 00:43:49,587
The Peoples Central
Air Defense Headquarters.

551
00:43:49,629 --> 00:43:51,965
Where is that, Dimitri?

552
00:43:52,007 --> 00:43:54,134
In Omsk. Right.

553
00:43:55,218 --> 00:43:56,469
Yes.

554
00:43:56,553 --> 00:43:59,472
You'll call them first, will you?

555
00:44:00,974 --> 00:44:03,893
Do you happen to have the phone number
on you, Dimitri?

556
00:44:05,770 --> 00:44:08,773
What? I see.
Just ask for Omsk information.

557
00:44:10,817 --> 00:44:14,946
I'm sorry too, Dimitri.
I'm very sorry.

558
00:44:15,030 --> 00:44:18,867
All right, you're sorrier than I am.
But I am sorry as well.

559
00:44:21,161 --> 00:44:23,455
I am as sorry as you are, Dimitri.

560
00:44:23,496 --> 00:44:25,498
Don't say that you're more sorry
than I am...

561
00:44:25,540 --> 00:44:28,501
because I'm capable of being
just as sorry as you are.

562
00:44:28,543 --> 00:44:30,503
So we're both sorry, all right?

563
00:44:30,545 --> 00:44:32,005
All right.

564
00:44:33,214 --> 00:44:37,510
Yes, he's right here. Yes, he wants
to talk to you. Just a second.

565
00:44:50,023 --> 00:44:51,733
What?

566
00:45:10,418 --> 00:45:13,296
What? What is it? What?

567
00:45:13,380 --> 00:45:16,383
The fools. The mad fools.

568
00:45:17,801 --> 00:45:19,969
What's happened?

569
00:45:20,053 --> 00:45:22,389
The doomsday machine.

570
00:45:22,430 --> 00:45:25,016
The doomsday machine?
What is that?

571
00:45:25,058 --> 00:45:30,480
A device which will destroy
all human and animal life on Earth.

572
00:45:30,563 --> 00:45:32,816
All human and animal life?

573
00:45:47,664 --> 00:45:49,958
- Mandrake?
- Yes, Jack?

574
00:45:51,251 --> 00:45:54,879
Have you ever seen a Commie
drink a glass of water?

575
00:45:54,921 --> 00:45:59,509
Well, I can't say I have, Jack.

576
00:46:00,719 --> 00:46:05,598
Vodka. That's what they drink,
isn't it? Never water.

577
00:46:05,640 --> 00:46:10,061
I believe that's what they drink, yes.

578
00:46:10,103 --> 00:46:13,565
On no account will a Commie
ever drink water...

579
00:46:13,648 --> 00:46:15,984
and not without good reason.

580
00:46:17,068 --> 00:46:19,738
Oh, yes.

581
00:46:19,779 --> 00:46:24,868
I can't quite see
what you're getting at.

582
00:46:25,994 --> 00:46:29,205
Water. That's what I'm getting at.
Water.

583
00:46:30,749 --> 00:46:34,210
Mandrake, water is the source
of all life.

584
00:46:35,754 --> 00:46:39,341
Seven-tenths of this Earth's surface
is water.

585
00:46:39,424 --> 00:46:42,761
Why, do you realize that...

586
00:46:42,802 --> 00:46:45,889
70% of you is water?

587
00:46:45,972 --> 00:46:47,390
Good Lord.

588
00:46:47,474 --> 00:46:52,604
And as human beings,
you and I need fresh, pure water...

589
00:46:52,645 --> 00:46:56,274
to replenish
our precious bodily fluids.

590
00:46:56,316 --> 00:46:59,069
- You beginning to understand?
- Yes.

591
00:47:06,409 --> 00:47:11,664
Have you never wondered why I drink
only distilled water...

592
00:47:11,748 --> 00:47:16,169
or rainwater,
and only pure grain alcohol?

593
00:47:16,211 --> 00:47:19,506
It did occur to me, Jack, yes.

594
00:47:20,632 --> 00:47:24,594
Have you ever heard of fluoridation
of water?

595
00:47:25,679 --> 00:47:29,516
Yes, I have heard of that, Jack, yes.

596
00:47:29,557 --> 00:47:31,518
Do you know what it is?

597
00:47:31,559 --> 00:47:34,688
No, no, I don't know what it is.

598
00:47:34,771 --> 00:47:38,692
Do you realize that fluoridation...

599
00:47:38,775 --> 00:47:41,611
is the most monstrously conceived...

600
00:47:41,695 --> 00:47:44,489
and dangerous Communist plot
we have ever had to face?

601
00:47:50,870 --> 00:47:52,872
Two can play at that game, soldier.

602
00:47:57,961 --> 00:48:00,672
That's nice shooting, soldier!

603
00:48:25,155 --> 00:48:27,198
Mandrake, come here.

604
00:48:27,282 --> 00:48:29,325
You calling me, Jack?

605
00:48:29,409 --> 00:48:31,828
Come over here
and help me with this belt.

606
00:48:34,873 --> 00:48:37,876
I haven't had very much experience...

607
00:48:37,917 --> 00:48:40,712
with those sort of machines.

608
00:48:40,795 --> 00:48:44,591
I've only ever pressed a button
in my old Spitfire.

609
00:48:44,674 --> 00:48:48,303
In the name of Her Majesty and the
Continental Congress, feed me this belt.

610
00:48:48,386 --> 00:48:53,141
Jack, I'd love to come,
but what's happened, you see...

611
00:48:53,224 --> 00:48:56,019
the string in my leg is gone.

612
00:48:57,103 --> 00:49:00,899
- The what?
- The string. I never told you.

613
00:49:00,940 --> 00:49:04,861
I've got a gammy leg.
Oh, dear. Gone. Shot off.

614
00:49:06,988 --> 00:49:10,658
Mandrake, come over here.
The redcoats are coming.

615
00:49:11,785 --> 00:49:15,914
When it is detonated, it will produce
enough radioactive fallout...

616
00:49:15,997 --> 00:49:17,957
so that in ten months...

617
00:49:17,999 --> 00:49:21,086
the surface of the Earth
will be as dead as the moon!

618
00:49:21,169 --> 00:49:24,130
Come on, De Sadesky!
That's ridiculous!

619
00:49:24,214 --> 00:49:28,343
Our studies show even the worst fallout
is down to a safe level after two weeks.

620
00:49:28,426 --> 00:49:33,431
- You never heard of cobalt thorium G.
- What about it?

621
00:49:33,515 --> 00:49:37,602
Cobalt thorium G has
a radioactive half-life of93 years.

622
00:49:37,686 --> 00:49:40,772
If you take 50 H bombs
in the 1 00 megaton range...

623
00:49:40,855 --> 00:49:43,274
and jacket them
with cobalt thorium G...

624
00:49:43,316 --> 00:49:47,946
when they are exploded,
they will produce a doomsday shroud...

625
00:49:48,029 --> 00:49:50,323
a lethal cloud of radioactivity...

626
00:49:50,407 --> 00:49:54,828
which will encircle the Earth
for 93 years!

627
00:49:54,911 --> 00:49:58,456
What a load of Commie bull.
I mean, after all.

628
00:49:59,541 --> 00:50:02,210
I'm afraid I don't understand
something, Alexi.

629
00:50:02,293 --> 00:50:05,922
Is the premier threatening to explode it
if our planes carry out their attack?

630
00:50:06,006 --> 00:50:08,550
No, sir. It is not a thing
a sane man would do.

631
00:50:08,633 --> 00:50:11,553
The doomsday machine is designed
to trigger itself automatically.

632
00:50:11,636 --> 00:50:13,888
Surely you can disarm it somehow.

633
00:50:13,972 --> 00:50:17,892
It is designed to explode if
any attempt is made to un-trigger it.

634
00:50:17,976 --> 00:50:19,227
Automatically?

635
00:50:19,310 --> 00:50:21,896
It's a Commie trick!
We're wasting valuable time!

636
00:50:21,980 --> 00:50:25,066
Look at the big board!
They're getting ready to clobber us!

637
00:50:25,150 --> 00:50:29,821
This is absolute madness.
Why should you build such a thing?

638
00:50:29,863 --> 00:50:31,865
There are those of us
who fought against it.

639
00:50:31,906 --> 00:50:33,992
But in the end, we could not keep up
with the expense involved...

640
00:50:34,034 --> 00:50:38,580
in the arms race, the space race
and the peace race.

641
00:50:38,663 --> 00:50:43,877
At the same time, our people grumbled
for more nylons and washing machines.

642
00:50:43,960 --> 00:50:46,504
Our doomsday scheme cost us
just a small fraction...

643
00:50:46,588 --> 00:50:49,841
of what we have been spending on defense
in a single year.

644
00:50:49,883 --> 00:50:54,346
The deciding factor was when we learned
your country was working similarly...

645
00:50:54,387 --> 00:50:56,348
and we were afraid of a doomsday gap!

646
00:50:56,389 --> 00:50:59,768
This is preposterous! I've never
approved of anything like that.

647
00:50:59,851 --> 00:51:02,687
Our source was The New York Times.

648
00:51:02,729 --> 00:51:06,649
Dr. Strangelove, do we have anything
like that in the works?

649
00:51:06,733 --> 00:51:09,194
A moment, please, Mr. President.

650
00:51:11,905 --> 00:51:15,367
Under the authority granted me...

651
00:51:15,408 --> 00:51:19,579
as director of weapons research
and development...

652
00:51:19,662 --> 00:51:23,875
I commissioned last year
a study of this project...

653
00:51:23,917 --> 00:51:26,169
by the Bland Corporation.

654
00:51:26,252 --> 00:51:29,381
Based on the findings of the report...

655
00:51:29,464 --> 00:51:34,969
my conclusion was that this idea
was not a practical deterrent...

656
00:51:35,053 --> 00:51:38,890
for reasons which at this moment
must be all too obvious.

657
00:51:38,932 --> 00:51:42,352
You mean it is possible for them
to have built such a thing?

658
00:51:46,523 --> 00:51:51,403
Mr. President, the technology required
is easily within the means...

659
00:51:51,444 --> 00:51:55,865
of even the smallest nuclear power.

660
00:51:55,949 --> 00:51:59,911
It requires only the will to do so.

661
00:52:00,912 --> 00:52:04,791
But how is it possible for this thing
to be triggered automatically...

662
00:52:04,833 --> 00:52:07,168
and at the same time
impossible to un-trigger?

663
00:52:07,252 --> 00:52:11,256
Mr. President,
it is not only possible...

664
00:52:11,339 --> 00:52:13,299
it is essential.

665
00:52:13,341 --> 00:52:17,804
That is the whole idea
of this machine, you know.

666
00:52:17,846 --> 00:52:23,059
Deterrence is the art of producing
in the mind of the enemy...

667
00:52:23,143 --> 00:52:25,729
the fear of attack.

668
00:52:25,812 --> 00:52:30,734
And so because of the automated and
irrevocable decision-making process...

669
00:52:30,817 --> 00:52:34,696
which rules out human meddling...

670
00:52:34,779 --> 00:52:38,742
the doomsday machine is terrifying...

671
00:52:38,825 --> 00:52:40,910
and simple to understand...

672
00:52:40,994 --> 00:52:44,664
and completely credible
and convincing.

673
00:52:44,748 --> 00:52:48,084
I wish we had one of them
doomsday machines.

674
00:52:48,168 --> 00:52:51,755
But this is fantastic, Strangelove.
How can it be triggered automatically?

675
00:52:51,838 --> 00:52:55,633
It's remarkably simple to do that.

676
00:52:55,675 --> 00:52:59,220
When you merely wish to bury bombs...

677
00:52:59,304 --> 00:53:01,639
there's no limit to the size.

678
00:53:01,681 --> 00:53:03,933
After that, they are connected...

679
00:53:04,017 --> 00:53:08,021
to a gigantic complex of computers.

680
00:53:08,104 --> 00:53:13,818
Now then, a specific and clearly
defined set of circumstances...

681
00:53:13,902 --> 00:53:17,364
under which the bombs
are to be exploded...

682
00:53:17,447 --> 00:53:21,493
is programmed into a tape memory bank.

683
00:53:21,534 --> 00:53:24,662
Hmm. Strangelove?

684
00:53:25,705 --> 00:53:28,792
What kind of a name is that?
That ain't no Kraut name, is it?

685
00:53:28,875 --> 00:53:31,169
He changed it when he became a citizen.

686
00:53:31,211 --> 00:53:34,214
It used to be Merkwurdichliebe.

687
00:53:34,297 --> 00:53:38,677
Well, a Kraut by any other name,
uh, Stainsey?

688
00:53:40,553 --> 00:53:44,933
The whole point of
the doomsday machine...

689
00:53:45,016 --> 00:53:48,561
is lost if you keep it a secret!

690
00:53:48,645 --> 00:53:50,814
Why didn't you tell the world?

691
00:53:50,897 --> 00:53:55,276
It was to be announced
at the Party Congress on Monday.

692
00:53:55,360 --> 00:53:58,697
As you know,
the premier loves surprises.

693
00:54:47,162 --> 00:54:49,414
Stay with me, Mandrake.

694
00:54:54,586 --> 00:54:57,255
All right, now feed me.
Feed me, boy.

695
00:55:27,160 --> 00:55:32,207
Don't you think we'd be better off
away from this flying glass?

696
00:55:32,290 --> 00:55:34,334
We're okay here.

697
00:55:36,002 --> 00:55:40,006
Mandrake, do you realize that
in addition to fluoridating the water...

698
00:55:40,090 --> 00:55:43,635
there are studies underway
to fluoridate salt, flour...

699
00:55:43,718 --> 00:55:48,765
fruit juices, soup, sugar,
milk, ice cream?

700
00:55:48,848 --> 00:55:50,100
Ice cream.

701
00:55:50,183 --> 00:55:52,602
- Children's ice cream.
- Good Lord.

702
00:55:52,686 --> 00:55:55,105
You know when fluoridation
first began?

703
00:55:56,147 --> 00:55:58,066
No, I don't, Jack.

704
00:55:58,149 --> 00:56:00,610
1 946.

705
00:56:00,694 --> 00:56:03,446
1 946, Mandrake.

706
00:56:03,530 --> 00:56:07,826
How does that coincide with
your postwar Commie conspiracy, huh?

707
00:56:07,867 --> 00:56:11,204
It's incredibly obvious, isn't it?

708
00:56:11,246 --> 00:56:16,793
A foreign substance is introduced
into our precious bodily fluids...

709
00:56:16,876 --> 00:56:20,130
without the knowledge
of the individual.

710
00:56:20,213 --> 00:56:22,132
Certainly without any choice.

711
00:56:23,925 --> 00:56:27,220
That's the way a hard-core Commie works.

712
00:56:28,680 --> 00:56:31,891
Jack. Tell me, Jack.

713
00:56:31,975 --> 00:56:34,644
When did you first become--

714
00:56:34,728 --> 00:56:37,480
Well, develop this theory?

715
00:56:38,565 --> 00:56:40,817
Well, l--

716
00:56:40,900 --> 00:56:44,446
I first became aware of it, Mandrake...

717
00:56:44,529 --> 00:56:46,531
during the physical act of love.

718
00:56:48,283 --> 00:56:52,537
Yes, a profound sense of fatigue...

719
00:56:52,620 --> 00:56:55,206
feeling of emptiness followed.

720
00:56:55,248 --> 00:56:59,044
Luckily I was able to interpret
these feelings correctly.

721
00:57:00,420 --> 00:57:02,047
Loss of essence.

722
00:57:03,715 --> 00:57:07,427
I can assure you it has not recurred,
Mandrake.

723
00:57:07,510 --> 00:57:10,430
Women sense my power...

724
00:57:11,681 --> 00:57:13,808
and they seek the life essence.

725
00:57:15,101 --> 00:57:18,438
I do not avoid women, Mandrake.

726
00:57:18,480 --> 00:57:21,399
But I do deny them my essence.

727
00:57:21,441 --> 00:57:24,319
Yes, yes, Jack.

728
00:57:36,956 --> 00:57:39,084
Cease fire!

729
00:58:00,397 --> 00:58:02,107
My boys must have surrendered.

730
00:58:02,148 --> 00:58:04,484
There it is.

731
00:58:04,567 --> 00:58:06,403
Jack, listen.

732
00:58:06,486 --> 00:58:09,823
While there's still time, I beg you,
let's recall the Wing and--

733
00:58:11,950 --> 00:58:14,786
Those boys were like my children.

734
00:58:16,329 --> 00:58:18,415
Now they let me down.

735
00:58:18,498 --> 00:58:20,166
No, not a bit.

736
00:58:20,250 --> 00:58:23,044
I'm sure they all gave it
their very best.

737
00:58:23,128 --> 00:58:25,630
I'm equally sure they all died
thinking of you...

738
00:58:25,672 --> 00:58:28,425
every man jack of them, Jack.

739
00:58:28,508 --> 00:58:31,136
Supposing a bit of water
has gone off, eh?

740
00:58:31,219 --> 00:58:33,513
Certainly one can never be too sure
about those things.

741
00:58:33,596 --> 00:58:36,558
But look at me.
Do I look all rancid and clotted?

742
00:58:36,641 --> 00:58:39,436
Look at me, Jack. Look.

743
00:58:39,519 --> 00:58:43,606
And I drink a lot of water.
I'm what you might call a water man.

744
00:58:43,690 --> 00:58:47,027
And I can swear to you, my boy,
swear to you...

745
00:58:47,110 --> 00:58:49,362
that there's nothing wrong
with my bodily fluids.

746
00:58:49,446 --> 00:58:51,948
Not a thing, Jackie.

747
00:58:52,032 --> 00:58:54,325
Mandrake, were you ever
a prisoner of war?

748
00:58:54,367 --> 00:58:58,038
Well, Jack, the time's running very--

749
00:58:58,121 --> 00:59:01,166
- What?
- Were you ever a prisoner of war?

750
00:59:01,249 --> 00:59:03,335
Yes, I was, as a matter of fact.

751
00:59:03,418 --> 00:59:06,504
Did they torture you?

752
00:59:06,588 --> 00:59:09,632
Yes, they did.
I was tortured by the Japanese.

753
00:59:09,716 --> 00:59:11,343
Not a pretty story.

754
00:59:11,426 --> 00:59:13,011
What happened?

755
00:59:13,094 --> 00:59:17,390
I don't know, Jack. It's difficult
to think under these conditions.

756
00:59:17,474 --> 00:59:19,684
Well, what happened was...

757
00:59:19,768 --> 00:59:23,188
they got me on the old
Rangoon-Inchinawa Railway.

758
00:59:23,229 --> 00:59:27,609
I was laying train lines
for the bloody Japanese puff-puffs.

759
00:59:27,692 --> 00:59:30,904
No, I mean, when they tortured you,
did you talk?

760
00:59:32,655 --> 00:59:34,657
No, l--

761
00:59:34,741 --> 00:59:38,995
Well, I don't think they wanted me
to talk, really, or say anything.

762
00:59:39,079 --> 00:59:42,165
It was their way of having
a bit of fun, the swine.

763
00:59:42,248 --> 00:59:45,585
The strange thing is,
they make such bloody good cameras.

764
00:59:47,295 --> 00:59:52,926
Those clowns outside will give me
a good going-over soon for the code.

765
00:59:55,929 --> 00:59:59,307
Yes, you may have quite a point
there, Jack.

766
01:00:00,433 --> 01:00:03,395
I don't know how well
I could stand up under torture.

767
01:00:03,478 --> 01:00:06,731
The answer to that is,
no one ever does.

768
01:00:06,815 --> 01:00:10,944
And my advise to you
is to give me the code now.

769
01:00:11,027 --> 01:00:13,947
If those devils come back
and try any rough stuff...

770
01:00:13,988 --> 01:00:17,242
we'll fight them together
like we did just now on the floor.

771
01:00:17,325 --> 01:00:20,870
You with your gun and me
with a belt of ammo, feeding you.

772
01:00:20,954 --> 01:00:23,748
" Feed me," you said,
and I was feeding you, Jack.

773
01:00:23,790 --> 01:00:26,459
You know, Mandrake...

774
01:00:26,543 --> 01:00:29,754
I happen to believe in
a life after this one...

775
01:00:31,297 --> 01:00:34,718
and I know I'll have to answer
for what I've done.

776
01:00:36,553 --> 01:00:38,013
And I think I can.

777
01:00:38,096 --> 01:00:41,307
Yes, of course you can.
Of course you can. You can.

778
01:00:41,391 --> 01:00:43,810
I'm a religious man myself,
you know.

779
01:00:43,893 --> 01:00:47,772
I believe in all that sort of thing
and I'm hoping, you know, Jack--

780
01:00:47,814 --> 01:00:50,692
You've dropped your gun, Jack.

781
01:00:50,775 --> 01:00:54,362
No, Jack, let me take that for you.

782
01:00:54,446 --> 01:00:57,949
You know what I'm hoping? I'm hoping
you're going to give me the code, boy.

783
01:00:59,701 --> 01:01:02,328
You're going to wash and brush up?
What a good idea.

784
01:01:02,412 --> 01:01:04,998
Always did wonders for a man,
a wash and brush up.

785
01:01:05,081 --> 01:01:07,834
Water on the back of the neck
makes you feel marvellous.

786
01:01:07,917 --> 01:01:10,670
That's what we need: water on
the back of the neck and the code.

787
01:01:10,754 --> 01:01:14,341
Supposing I play a little guessing game
with you, Jack boy?

788
01:01:14,424 --> 01:01:17,427
I'll try and guess
what the code is--

789
01:01:33,902 --> 01:01:38,406
Copilot to navigator.
I'm ready with the fuel figures now.

790
01:01:38,490 --> 01:01:41,451
We have 1 09,000 total...

791
01:01:41,534 --> 01:01:44,371
79,000in the mains...

792
01:01:44,412 --> 01:01:47,207
and30,000in the auxiliaries.

793
01:01:47,290 --> 01:01:49,209
And that works out
toroughly...

794
01:01:49,292 --> 01:01:52,754
seven hours, 15minutes
endurance from this time.

795
01:01:53,880 --> 01:01:55,340
D.S.O. to Captain.

796
01:01:55,382 --> 01:01:58,510
I have an unidentified
radar blip.

797
01:01:59,886 --> 01:02:02,514
Distance: 60 miles.

798
01:02:03,682 --> 01:02:06,851
Approximate speed:
Mach three.

799
01:02:06,893 --> 01:02:08,853
Looks like
a missile tracking us.

800
01:02:11,773 --> 01:02:13,858
Confirmed:
definite missile track.

801
01:02:13,900 --> 01:02:15,985
Commence evasive action right.

802
01:02:22,242 --> 01:02:25,870
Missile still closing range.

803
01:02:25,954 --> 01:02:29,958
Distance: 50 miles.
Continue evasive action.

804
01:02:30,041 --> 01:02:32,752
Lock E.C.M. to target intercept mode.

805
01:02:32,836 --> 01:02:36,464
E.C.M. locked to
target intercept mode.

806
01:02:36,548 --> 01:02:38,967
Missile still tracking
and closing distance.

807
01:02:39,050 --> 01:02:43,054
Range: 40 miles.
Continue evasive action.

808
01:02:45,932 --> 01:02:50,228
Electronic Guidance Scrambler
to blue grid.

809
01:02:50,270 --> 01:02:53,773
Missile still tracking steady
and closing distance.

810
01:02:53,857 --> 01:02:55,775
Range: 30 miles.

811
01:02:58,069 --> 01:03:02,282
Missile still closing true and steady.
Continue evasive action.

812
01:03:09,831 --> 01:03:11,833
Range: 20 miles.

813
01:03:11,916 --> 01:03:15,795
Missile still closing distance
and tracking steady.

814
01:03:15,837 --> 01:03:18,298
Attack range gate
on maximum scan.

815
01:03:18,340 --> 01:03:20,800
Range gate on maximum scan.

816
01:03:20,842 --> 01:03:23,720
Range: 10 miles.

817
01:03:23,803 --> 01:03:27,766
Missile track deflecting.
Continue evasive action.

818
01:03:27,807 --> 01:03:31,102
Deflection increasing.
Range: eight miles.

819
01:03:31,144 --> 01:03:35,106
Deflection still increasing.
Range: six miles.

820
01:03:35,148 --> 01:03:37,859
Missile still deflecting.
Range: four miles.

821
01:03:43,656 --> 01:03:46,868
Range: two miles.
Missile still deflecting.

822
01:03:46,951 --> 01:03:49,204
Range: one mile.
Missile detonated!

823
01:03:55,877 --> 01:03:57,962
- Start lever to cut off!.
- Cut off!.

824
01:04:01,383 --> 01:04:02,842
We're losin' power!

825
01:04:11,267 --> 01:04:13,603
Re-select essential power!

826
01:04:13,687 --> 01:04:15,689
Essential power re-selected.

827
01:04:22,320 --> 01:04:24,239
The hatch is stuck!

828
01:04:27,826 --> 01:04:29,244
Hit emergency power!

829
01:04:31,746 --> 01:04:34,582
- Extinguishers!
- Roger!

830
01:04:41,339 --> 01:04:44,592
- Transfer switches!
- Transferred!

831
01:04:44,676 --> 01:04:46,928
- Boost pumps off!.
- Cut off!.

832
01:04:58,690 --> 01:05:00,692
Fuel valves three, four and six!

833
01:05:13,204 --> 01:05:14,622
Give me full power!

834
01:05:27,510 --> 01:05:30,096
Peace on Earth.

835
01:05:34,768 --> 01:05:37,437
P.O.E.

836
01:05:37,520 --> 01:05:40,398
Purity of Essence.

837
01:05:40,440 --> 01:05:43,985
O.P.O.E.

838
01:05:55,121 --> 01:05:57,457
Put your hands over your head.

839
01:05:57,540 --> 01:06:00,168
What do you think you're doing?
Who are you?

840
01:06:00,251 --> 01:06:02,128
Put your hands over your head.

841
01:06:02,170 --> 01:06:05,757
What kind of suit
do you call that, fella?

842
01:06:05,840 --> 01:06:07,842
What do you mean, suit?

843
01:06:07,926 --> 01:06:10,345
This happens to be
an R.A.F. uniform...

844
01:06:10,428 --> 01:06:14,766
and I am Group Captain Lionel Mandrake,
General Ripper's executive officer.

845
01:06:14,808 --> 01:06:16,351
Where's General Ripper?

846
01:06:16,434 --> 01:06:19,270
He's dead, in the bathroom.

847
01:06:19,312 --> 01:06:21,481
Where's the bathroom?

848
01:06:21,564 --> 01:06:22,982
Next to you.

849
01:06:32,492 --> 01:06:35,203
I don't know what stupid game
this is you're playing...

850
01:06:35,286 --> 01:06:37,414
but I've got a good idea
what the recall code is...

851
01:06:37,497 --> 01:06:40,000
and I have to get in touch
with SAC headquarters immediately!

852
01:06:40,083 --> 01:06:43,795
Put your hands over your head
and keep 'em there! Go on.

853
01:06:43,837 --> 01:06:45,547
Got any witnesses?

854
01:06:45,630 --> 01:06:47,549
What are you talking about?
He shot himself!.

855
01:06:47,632 --> 01:06:49,634
While he was shavin'?

856
01:06:49,718 --> 01:06:52,887
Now look, Colonel Bat Guano...

857
01:06:52,971 --> 01:06:55,432
if that really is your name...

858
01:06:55,515 --> 01:06:59,352
may I tell you that I have
a very good idea--

859
01:06:59,436 --> 01:07:02,480
I think, hope, pray--
what the recall code is.

860
01:07:02,522 --> 01:07:05,275
It's some theme he kept repeating.
A variation on...

861
01:07:05,358 --> 01:07:08,570
" Peace on Earth" or " Purity of Essence,"
one of those.

862
01:07:08,653 --> 01:07:12,490
Put your hands on top of your head.
Start walkin'.

863
01:07:12,532 --> 01:07:15,785
Don't you know that General Ripper
went mad...

864
01:07:15,869 --> 01:07:19,247
and sent the whole Wing
to attack the Soviets?

865
01:07:19,330 --> 01:07:22,834
- What are you talkin' about?
- I'll tell you what I'm talking about.

866
01:07:22,917 --> 01:07:27,005
I'm going to pick up this red telephone,
which is connected to SAC...

867
01:07:27,088 --> 01:07:28,548
and I hope--

868
01:07:30,050 --> 01:07:32,218
Blast. Blast.

869
01:07:32,302 --> 01:07:36,306
Shot away, I expect, by one of your men
during this ridiculous fighting!

870
01:07:37,724 --> 01:07:39,768
Right.

871
01:07:39,851 --> 01:07:43,229
All right, Charlie, I've been
wastin' too much time on you.

872
01:07:43,313 --> 01:07:47,108
I got a lot of wounded men outside.
Start walkin'.

873
01:08:09,422 --> 01:08:13,259
All the radio gear is out,
including the C.R.M. 114.

874
01:08:13,301 --> 01:08:16,471
I think the auto-destruct mechanism
got hit and blew itself up.

875
01:08:20,975 --> 01:08:24,229
The fire is out.
The emergency power is on.

876
01:08:24,270 --> 01:08:27,774
Everything checks out all right.
Will advise.

877
01:08:27,857 --> 01:08:29,567
Roger. Navigator?

878
01:08:29,651 --> 01:08:35,115
I've worked out our rate of fuel loss
at approximately 1 -6-2 per minute.

879
01:08:35,198 --> 01:08:37,992
This gives us a radius of action
sufficient to take out...

880
01:08:38,076 --> 01:08:41,454
primary and secondary targets,
but we will not...

881
01:08:41,496 --> 01:08:45,667
repeat, not be able to make it back
to any base or neutral country.

882
01:08:46,626 --> 01:08:49,170
However, we would have
enough fuel to ditch...

883
01:08:49,254 --> 01:08:51,965
at weather ship Tango Delta...

884
01:08:52,048 --> 01:08:55,301
grid coordinates 0-0-3-6-9-1.

885
01:09:00,098 --> 01:09:02,517
Well, boys,
we got three engines out.

886
01:09:02,600 --> 01:09:06,396
We got more holes in us
than a horse trader's mule.

887
01:09:06,479 --> 01:09:08,481
The radio is gone,
and we're leakin' fuel.

888
01:09:08,565 --> 01:09:11,985
And if we was flyin' any lower,
we'd need sleigh bells on this thing.

889
01:09:12,068 --> 01:09:15,071
But we got one little budge
on them Ruskies.

890
01:09:15,155 --> 01:09:17,073
At this height
they might harpoon us...

891
01:09:17,157 --> 01:09:20,243
but they sure ain't gonna spot us
on no radar screen.

892
01:09:31,421 --> 01:09:33,340
The other way.

893
01:09:33,423 --> 01:09:35,842
- Where are you taking me?
- To the main gate.

894
01:09:37,886 --> 01:09:41,348
Colonel, I must know what you think
has been going on here.

895
01:09:41,431 --> 01:09:43,350
- You wanna know what I think?
- Yes.

896
01:09:43,433 --> 01:09:46,144
I think you're some kind
of deviated "prevert."

897
01:09:46,186 --> 01:09:48,938
I think General Ripper found out
about your "preversion"...

898
01:09:49,022 --> 01:09:51,316
and that you were organizing
some kind of mutiny of "preverts."

899
01:09:51,358 --> 01:09:53,777
Now, move!

900
01:09:53,860 --> 01:09:57,155
On top of that, I don't know anything
about any planes attacking Russia.

901
01:09:57,238 --> 01:10:01,034
I was told to get Ripper on the phone
with the President of the United States.

902
01:10:01,117 --> 01:10:05,872
Now just one second.
You just said "the president."

903
01:10:05,955 --> 01:10:08,166
What about the president?

904
01:10:08,249 --> 01:10:11,419
The president wants to speak
to General Ripper, doesn't he?

905
01:10:11,503 --> 01:10:14,089
Now, General Ripper is dead,
is he not?

906
01:10:14,172 --> 01:10:16,383
I am General Ripper's
executive officer...

907
01:10:16,466 --> 01:10:19,427
so the president will want
to speak to me, won't he?

908
01:10:19,511 --> 01:10:23,223
There's a telephone box over there
and the line may be open.

909
01:10:23,306 --> 01:10:26,101
You wanna talk to
the President of the United States?

910
01:10:26,184 --> 01:10:29,062
I don't want to talk to him, Colonel,
I've got to talk to him.

911
01:10:29,104 --> 01:10:32,774
And if you don't put that gun away
and stop this stupid nonsense...

912
01:10:32,857 --> 01:10:36,861
the Court of Inquiry on this
will give you such a pranging...

913
01:10:36,945 --> 01:10:41,032
you'll be lucky to end up wearing the
uniform of a bloody toilet attendant!

914
01:10:45,870 --> 01:10:49,499
Go ahead, try and get the President
of the United States on the phone.

915
01:10:52,168 --> 01:10:54,212
Try any "preversions,"
I'll blow your head off.

916
01:11:08,852 --> 01:11:11,688
Operator? This is
Group Captain Lionel Mandrake.

917
01:11:11,771 --> 01:11:13,815
I'm speaking from
Burpelson Air Force Base.

918
01:11:13,898 --> 01:11:17,777
Something urgent has come up and I want
you to place a person-to-person call...

919
01:11:17,861 --> 01:11:20,947
with President Merkin Muffley
in the Pentagon, Washington, D.C.

920
01:11:22,323 --> 01:11:25,535
Burpelson3-9-1-8-0.

921
01:11:26,745 --> 01:11:31,791
No, I'm perfectly serious.
The President of the United States.

922
01:11:31,875 --> 01:11:34,794
I'm sorry,
I haven't got enough change.

923
01:11:34,836 --> 01:11:38,298
Could you make this
a collect call, Operator?

924
01:11:50,226 --> 01:11:53,855
Just one second, Operator.
They won't accept the call.

925
01:11:53,938 --> 01:11:55,815
Have you got 55 cents?

926
01:11:55,899 --> 01:11:58,943
Do you think I'd go into combat
with loose change in my pocket?

927
01:12:01,321 --> 01:12:04,199
Operator, look.

928
01:12:04,282 --> 01:12:07,744
Is it possible to make this
an ordinary trunk call?

929
01:12:07,827 --> 01:12:10,622
Well, what do you call it?
You know--

930
01:12:10,663 --> 01:12:13,667
Oh, station-to-station.

931
01:12:17,796 --> 01:12:21,299
Oh, blast!
I'm still 20 cents short.

932
01:12:23,176 --> 01:12:26,596
Operator, hold on.
I shan't keep you a second.

933
01:12:26,680 --> 01:12:30,809
Colonel, that Coca-Cola machine.
I want you to shoot the lock off it.

934
01:12:30,892 --> 01:12:32,977
There may be change in there.

935
01:12:36,523 --> 01:12:37,982
That's private property.

936
01:12:38,024 --> 01:12:40,985
Can you possibly imagine
what is going to happen to you...

937
01:12:41,027 --> 01:12:43,738
your frame outlook,
way of life and everything...

938
01:12:43,822 --> 01:12:48,326
when they learn you have obstructed
a phone call to the president?

939
01:12:48,410 --> 01:12:52,414
Can you imagine?
Shoot it off!.

940
01:12:52,497 --> 01:12:56,126
Shoot with the gun! That's what
the bullets are for, you twit!

941
01:12:56,209 --> 01:12:59,629
Okay, I'm gonna get
your money for you.

942
01:12:59,713 --> 01:13:03,842
But if you don't get the president on
the phone, you know what's gonna happen?

943
01:13:03,925 --> 01:13:07,512
You're gonna have to answer
to the Coca-Cola Company.

944
01:13:16,855 --> 01:13:19,774
This is SAC
Communications Control.

945
01:13:19,858 --> 01:13:23,236
There call code O.P.E...

946
01:13:23,319 --> 01:13:25,238
is being acknowledged "roger"...

947
01:13:25,321 --> 01:13:30,243
by elements of
the 8-4-3 Bomb Wing.

948
01:13:30,285 --> 01:13:32,287
These are the details.

949
01:13:32,370 --> 01:13:36,916
Missions 12, 22, 30and38...

950
01:13:37,000 --> 01:13:40,545
are reported destroyed
by enemy action.

951
01:13:40,628 --> 01:13:45,216
All other missions have
acknowledged recall code.

952
01:13:45,300 --> 01:13:47,260
This is SAC Communications Control.

953
01:13:47,302 --> 01:13:48,970
Over and out.

954
01:13:49,054 --> 01:13:50,930
Gentlemen, gentlemen.

955
01:13:51,014 --> 01:13:53,433
Gentlemen.

956
01:13:53,475 --> 01:13:55,435
Mr. President.

957
01:13:55,477 --> 01:13:57,562
I'm not a sentimentalist by nature...

958
01:13:57,645 --> 01:14:00,899
but I think I know what's
in every heart in this room.

959
01:14:00,982 --> 01:14:04,819
I think we all ought
to bow our heads...

960
01:14:04,903 --> 01:14:06,946
and give a prayer of thanks
for our deliverance.

961
01:14:07,030 --> 01:14:08,448
Lord...

962
01:14:09,699 --> 01:14:14,287
we have heard the wings
of the Angel of Death...

963
01:14:14,371 --> 01:14:17,248
fluttering over our heads
from the Valley of Fear.

964
01:14:17,290 --> 01:14:19,959
You have seen fit to deliver us
from the forces of evil--

965
01:14:20,043 --> 01:14:21,628
Excuse me, sir.

966
01:14:21,711 --> 01:14:24,839
Premier Kissoff's calling again
and he's hopping mad.

967
01:14:31,596 --> 01:14:35,517
Fuel flow on active engines
and leakage has increased.

968
01:14:35,600 --> 01:14:39,604
Now works out at 2-0-5.

969
01:14:40,689 --> 01:14:42,691
Estimate remaining fuel...

970
01:14:42,774 --> 01:14:46,653
at8-7-9-0.

971
01:14:49,989 --> 01:14:53,868
Roger.
Confirm 2-0-5 per minute...

972
01:14:53,952 --> 01:14:57,997
and remaining fuel8-7-9-0.

973
01:15:04,504 --> 01:15:08,633
No, no, Dimitri,
there must be some mistake.

974
01:15:08,675 --> 01:15:10,760
No, I'm certain of that.

975
01:15:10,844 --> 01:15:15,015
I'm perfectly certain
of that, Dimitri.

976
01:15:15,098 --> 01:15:18,018
Just a second.
You know what he says?

977
01:15:18,059 --> 01:15:20,311
He says one of the planes
hasn't turned back.

978
01:15:20,395 --> 01:15:22,981
He says according to information
forwarded by our Air Staffs...

979
01:15:23,064 --> 01:15:26,026
it's headed for
the missile complex at Laputa.

980
01:15:29,029 --> 01:15:31,948
That's impossible, Mr. President.

981
01:15:32,032 --> 01:15:34,075
I mean,
look at the big board.

982
01:15:34,159 --> 01:15:37,287
Thirty-four planes, 30 recalls
acknowledged and four splashes...

983
01:15:37,370 --> 01:15:40,206
and one of them
was targeted for Laputa.

984
01:15:43,168 --> 01:15:46,338
Dimitri, look, we've got
an acknowledgement from every plane...

985
01:15:46,421 --> 01:15:49,674
except the four you've shot down.

986
01:15:57,057 --> 01:15:59,434
Hang on a second, Dimitri.

987
01:15:59,517 --> 01:16:02,854
He says their air defense now only
claims three aircraft confirmed.

988
01:16:02,896 --> 01:16:05,398
The fourth may only be damaged.

989
01:16:07,567 --> 01:16:09,486
Mr. President...

990
01:16:09,569 --> 01:16:11,905
I'm beginnin' to smell
a big, fat Commie rat.

991
01:16:11,988 --> 01:16:15,867
I mean, supposin' Kissoff is lyin'
about that fourth plane...

992
01:16:15,909 --> 01:16:18,078
just lookin' for
an excuse to clobber us?

993
01:16:18,161 --> 01:16:20,580
If the spaghetti hits the fan,
we're in trouble.

994
01:16:24,709 --> 01:16:27,295
Dimitri, look,
if this report is true...

995
01:16:27,379 --> 01:16:31,007
and the plane manages
to bomb the target...

996
01:16:31,091 --> 01:16:35,303
is this gonna set off
the doomsday machine?

997
01:16:38,556 --> 01:16:40,517
Are you sure?

998
01:16:41,726 --> 01:16:46,272
Well, I guess you're just gonna have
to get that plane, Dimitri.

999
01:16:46,356 --> 01:16:49,401
I'm sorry they're jamming
your radar and flying so low...

1000
01:16:49,484 --> 01:16:51,695
but they're trained to do it.

1001
01:16:51,778 --> 01:16:53,405
It's initiative.

1002
01:16:55,115 --> 01:16:57,992
Look, Dimitri, you know
exactly where they're going...

1003
01:16:58,076 --> 01:17:01,246
and I'm sure your entire air defense
can stop a single plane.

1004
01:17:04,416 --> 01:17:09,004
It's not gonna help either one of us
if the doomsday machine goes off, is it?

1005
01:17:10,547 --> 01:17:15,802
There's no point in you getting
hysterical at a moment like this!

1006
01:17:15,885 --> 01:17:20,098
Keep your feet on the ground
when you're talking, Dimitri.

1007
01:17:20,181 --> 01:17:22,434
I am not--
I am not getting--

1008
01:17:22,517 --> 01:17:24,978
No, Dimitri, I'm just worried.

1009
01:17:25,020 --> 01:17:26,938
That's all.

1010
01:17:26,980 --> 01:17:30,066
Now look, if our Air Staffs say
its primary target is Laputa...

1011
01:17:30,150 --> 01:17:34,070
and its secondary target is Borchov,
it's true.

1012
01:17:34,154 --> 01:17:35,613
You gotta believe it!

1013
01:17:35,655 --> 01:17:39,409
Dimitri, can I give you
just one word--

1014
01:17:39,492 --> 01:17:42,787
Can I give you just one word
of advice, Dimitri?

1015
01:17:42,871 --> 01:17:44,539
Listen, Dimitri.

1016
01:17:44,622 --> 01:17:48,168
Put everything you've got into
those two sectors, and you can't miss!

1017
01:17:54,549 --> 01:17:58,219
Sir, if we continue to lose fuel
at the present rate...

1018
01:17:58,303 --> 01:18:02,432
I estimate we only have
38 minutes flying time...

1019
01:18:02,515 --> 01:18:04,976
which will not even take us
as far as the primary.

1020
01:18:05,018 --> 01:18:08,980
Doggone it, Sweets, you told me that
you could get me to the primary!

1021
01:18:09,022 --> 01:18:12,859
I'm sorry, sir. That estimate was based
on the original loss rate factor...

1022
01:18:12,942 --> 01:18:14,736
not at 2-0-5.

1023
01:18:14,819 --> 01:18:17,072
I don't give a hoot in hell
how you do it...

1024
01:18:17,155 --> 01:18:19,324
you just get me to
the primary, you hear?

1025
01:18:19,366 --> 01:18:22,827
I'm sorry, sir,
but those are the figures.

1026
01:18:22,869 --> 01:18:26,164
We'll be lucky to reach
weather ship at Tango Delta.

1027
01:18:26,206 --> 01:18:28,416
Well, shoot!

1028
01:18:28,500 --> 01:18:32,837
We ain't come this far just
to dump this thing in the drink.

1029
01:18:32,879 --> 01:18:34,881
What's the nearest
target of opportunity?

1030
01:18:43,682 --> 01:18:46,393
Sir, if the rate of loss
does not increase...

1031
01:18:46,476 --> 01:18:50,230
we have a chance
to reach target 3-8-4...

1032
01:18:50,313 --> 01:18:55,151
grid coordinate 0-0-3-6-9-1 ...

1033
01:18:55,235 --> 01:18:59,072
and possibly make it from there
to the Tango Delta weather ship.

1034
01:18:59,155 --> 01:19:01,282
What kind of a target
is that, anyhow?

1035
01:19:01,366 --> 01:19:05,286
Sir, that's the I.C.B.M.
complex at Kotloss.

1036
01:19:05,370 --> 01:19:11,084
All right.
Designating new target: 3-8-4.

1037
01:19:11,167 --> 01:19:14,170
Give me a headin' on that just as soon
as you get it worked out.

1038
01:19:26,349 --> 01:19:31,229
We'll keep our fingers crossed.
Remember, we're all in this together.

1039
01:19:31,271 --> 01:19:35,108
We're right behind you,
we're with you all the way.

1040
01:19:35,191 --> 01:19:38,903
Yes. We'll keep the line open.

1041
01:19:38,987 --> 01:19:40,447
All right, Dimitri.

1042
01:19:42,782 --> 01:19:44,242
General Turgidson...

1043
01:19:44,284 --> 01:19:47,537
is there really a chance
for that plane to get through?

1044
01:19:49,247 --> 01:19:51,666
Mr. President,
if I may speak freely.

1045
01:19:51,750 --> 01:19:55,378
The Ruskie talks big, but frankly
we think he's short of know-how.

1046
01:19:55,462 --> 01:19:59,924
You can't expect ignorant peons
to understand a machine like our boys.

1047
01:20:00,008 --> 01:20:02,469
That's not meant as an insult,
Mr. Ambassador.

1048
01:20:02,510 --> 01:20:05,096
We all know how much guts
the average Ruskie's got.

1049
01:20:05,180 --> 01:20:08,308
Look at all of them Nazis killed
off, and they still wouldn't quit!

1050
01:20:08,391 --> 01:20:10,310
Can't you stick to the point?

1051
01:20:10,352 --> 01:20:14,105
Well, sir,
if the pilot's good, see--

1052
01:20:14,147 --> 01:20:18,318
I mean, if he's really sharp,
he can barrel that baby in so low.

1053
01:20:18,401 --> 01:20:22,906
You oughta see it! It's a sight!
A big plane like a 52! Vroom!

1054
01:20:22,989 --> 01:20:26,034
Its jet exhaust fryin' chickens
in the barnyard!

1055
01:20:26,117 --> 01:20:29,245
- But has he got a chance?
- Has he got a chance?

1056
01:20:29,329 --> 01:20:30,747
Hell, ye--

1057
01:20:56,231 --> 01:20:57,691
Navigator to Captain.

1058
01:20:57,732 --> 01:21:02,278
Approaching target
at distance 1-0 miles.

1059
01:21:02,362 --> 01:21:05,657
Switch from green grid
to target orange.

1060
01:21:05,740 --> 01:21:08,827
Roger.
Ready for final bomb run check.

1061
01:21:08,910 --> 01:21:10,370
- Take over, Ace.
- Roger.

1062
01:21:15,625 --> 01:21:18,128
- D.S.O. ready.
- Bombardier ready, sir.

1063
01:21:18,211 --> 01:21:20,380
Bomb fusing, master safety on.

1064
01:21:20,463 --> 01:21:23,550
Electronic, barometric,
time and impact.

1065
01:21:23,633 --> 01:21:25,969
Bomb fusing,
master safeties on.

1066
01:21:26,052 --> 01:21:29,097
Electronic, barometric,
time and impact.

1067
01:21:29,180 --> 01:21:32,767
Fuse for ground burst.
Delay factor yellow three.

1068
01:21:32,851 --> 01:21:35,478
Fuse for ground burst.
Delay factor yellow three.

1069
01:21:35,562 --> 01:21:38,314
Bomb fusing circuits
one through four, test.

1070
01:21:38,398 --> 01:21:41,985
Bomb fusing circuits one through four,
test. Lights on.

1071
01:21:42,068 --> 01:21:44,988
Bomb arming test lights on,
one through four.

1072
01:21:45,071 --> 01:21:47,907
Bomb arming test lights on,
one through four.

1073
01:21:47,991 --> 01:21:50,702
Engage primary trigger switch override.

1074
01:21:50,744 --> 01:21:53,872
Primary trigger switch override engaged.

1075
01:21:53,955 --> 01:21:56,541
Track indicators
to maximum deflection.

1076
01:21:56,583 --> 01:21:59,044
Track indicators
to maximum deflection.

1077
01:21:59,085 --> 01:22:02,297
Detonator set to zero altitude.

1078
01:22:02,380 --> 01:22:05,133
Detonator set to zero altitude.

1079
01:22:05,216 --> 01:22:06,885
Release first safety.

1080
01:22:11,181 --> 01:22:13,099
First safety released.

1081
01:22:14,476 --> 01:22:17,896
- First safety.
- Release second safety.

1082
01:22:20,690 --> 01:22:22,609
Second safety released.

1083
01:22:24,069 --> 01:22:25,487
Second safety.

1084
01:22:33,036 --> 01:22:35,705
Check bomb door circuits
one through four.

1085
01:22:46,299 --> 01:22:49,719
Uh, bomb door circuits...

1086
01:22:49,803 --> 01:22:52,430
negative function, lights red.

1087
01:22:52,514 --> 01:22:55,100
-Switch in backup circuits.
- Roger.

1088
01:22:55,183 --> 01:22:59,145
Backup circuits switched in.
Still negative function.

1089
01:22:59,229 --> 01:23:00,980
Engage emergency power.

1090
01:23:01,064 --> 01:23:03,400
Roger.

1091
01:23:03,483 --> 01:23:05,819
Emergency power on.
Still negative function.

1092
01:23:07,862 --> 01:23:09,906
Operate manual override!

1093
01:23:11,491 --> 01:23:13,034
Roger.

1094
01:23:22,627 --> 01:23:25,088
Still negative function.

1095
01:23:25,171 --> 01:23:27,924
The Teleflex drive cable
must be sheared away.

1096
01:23:28,008 --> 01:23:32,137
- Fire the explosive bolts!
- Roger.

1097
01:23:46,693 --> 01:23:50,321
Still negative, sir.
The operating circuits are dead, sir.

1098
01:23:55,744 --> 01:23:59,706
Stay on the bomb run, Ace. I'm goin'
down below and see what I can do.

1099
01:24:12,635 --> 01:24:14,095
Stay on the bomb run.

1100
01:24:14,179 --> 01:24:18,350
I'm gonna get them doors open
if it harelips everybody on Bear Creek!

1101
01:25:11,945 --> 01:25:14,823
Target orange grid reference checks.

1102
01:25:14,906 --> 01:25:17,200
Target distance: eight miles.

1103
01:25:17,283 --> 01:25:19,369
Roger. Eight miles.

1104
01:25:19,452 --> 01:25:21,746
Telemetric guidance computer
into orange grid.

1105
01:25:21,830 --> 01:25:24,290
Telemetric guidance computer
into orange grid.

1106
01:25:32,924 --> 01:25:35,468
Target distance: seven miles.

1107
01:25:35,552 --> 01:25:38,888
Correct track indicator:
minus seven.

1108
01:25:38,972 --> 01:25:42,559
Roger. Seven miles.
Check G.P.I. acceleration factor.

1109
01:25:42,642 --> 01:25:44,644
G.P.I. acceleration factor set.

1110
01:25:48,064 --> 01:25:50,525
Target distance: six miles.

1111
01:25:50,608 --> 01:25:55,238
Roger. Six miles.
Pulse ident transponder active.

1112
01:25:55,321 --> 01:25:56,865
Pulse ident transponder active.

1113
01:26:03,997 --> 01:26:07,000
Target distance: five miles.

1114
01:26:07,083 --> 01:26:11,046
Five miles. Homing alignment
factor to zero mode.

1115
01:26:11,129 --> 01:26:13,131
Homing alignment factor
to zero mode.

1116
01:26:16,718 --> 01:26:19,262
Target distance: four miles.

1117
01:26:19,346 --> 01:26:21,014
Roger. Four miles.

1118
01:26:21,097 --> 01:26:24,017
Auto C.D.C. into
manual Teleflex link.

1119
01:26:24,059 --> 01:26:26,644
Auto C.D.C. into
manual Teleflex link.

1120
01:26:36,905 --> 01:26:39,449
Target distance: three miles.

1121
01:26:39,532 --> 01:26:41,993
Roger. Three miles.

1122
01:26:42,077 --> 01:26:45,747
Target in sight!
Where in hell is Major Kong?

1123
01:27:09,521 --> 01:27:10,772
What about Major Kong?

1124
01:27:38,967 --> 01:27:42,679
Mr. President, I would not
rule out the chance...

1125
01:27:42,762 --> 01:27:45,807
to preserve a nucleus
of human specimens.

1126
01:27:45,890 --> 01:27:48,768
It would be quite easy...

1127
01:27:51,187 --> 01:27:56,276
at the bottom of some
of our deeper mine shafts.

1128
01:27:56,359 --> 01:28:01,197
The radioactivity would never penetrate
a mine some thousands of feet deep.

1129
01:28:01,281 --> 01:28:05,535
And in a matter of weeks, sufficient
improvements in dwelling space...

1130
01:28:05,618 --> 01:28:07,537
could easily be provided.

1131
01:28:07,620 --> 01:28:10,373
How long would you have
to stay down there?

1132
01:28:10,457 --> 01:28:14,294
Well, that's, you know--

1133
01:28:14,377 --> 01:28:17,047
Cobalt thorium G.

1134
01:28:27,307 --> 01:28:31,102
Radioactive half-life of--

1135
01:28:33,188 --> 01:28:37,942
I would think that possibly
one hundred years.

1136
01:28:40,278 --> 01:28:44,240
You mean, people could actually
stay down there for 100 years?

1137
01:28:44,324 --> 01:28:46,576
It would not be difficult,
Mein Fuhrer.

1138
01:28:46,659 --> 01:28:48,870
Nuclear reactors could--

1139
01:28:48,953 --> 01:28:51,289
I'm sorry, Mr. President.

1140
01:28:51,373 --> 01:28:55,168
Nuclear reactors could provide
power almost indefinitely.

1141
01:28:55,251 --> 01:28:58,088
Greenhouses could maintain
plant life.

1142
01:28:58,171 --> 01:29:01,758
Animals could be bred
and slaughtered.

1143
01:29:01,841 --> 01:29:06,262
A quick survey would have to be made of
the available mine sites in the country.

1144
01:29:06,346 --> 01:29:10,141
But I would guess
that a dwelling space...

1145
01:29:10,183 --> 01:29:13,853
for several hundred thousand of
our people could easily be provided.

1146
01:29:13,937 --> 01:29:17,065
Well, I would hate
to have to decide...

1147
01:29:17,148 --> 01:29:20,026
who stays up and who goes down.

1148
01:29:20,110 --> 01:29:24,030
Well, that would not be
necessary, Mr. President.

1149
01:29:24,072 --> 01:29:26,950
It could easily be accomplished
with a computer.

1150
01:29:27,033 --> 01:29:29,327
And the computer could
be set and programmed...

1151
01:29:29,369 --> 01:29:32,455
to accept factors
from youth, health...

1152
01:29:32,539 --> 01:29:35,667
sexual fertility, intelligence...

1153
01:29:35,750 --> 01:29:38,253
and a cross-section
of necessary skills.

1154
01:29:38,336 --> 01:29:40,588
Of course, it would be
absolutely vital...

1155
01:29:40,672 --> 01:29:44,634
that our top government
and military men be included...

1156
01:29:44,718 --> 01:29:49,514
to foster and impart the required
principles of leadership and tradition.

1157
01:29:55,562 --> 01:29:58,523
Naturally, they would breed
prodigiously.

1158
01:29:58,565 --> 01:30:01,359
There would be much time
and little to do.

1159
01:30:02,986 --> 01:30:07,907
But with the proper breeding techniques
and a ratio of, say...

1160
01:30:07,991 --> 01:30:10,744
ten females to each male...

1161
01:30:10,827 --> 01:30:15,457
they could then work their way back
to the present gross national product...

1162
01:30:15,540 --> 01:30:17,292
within 20 years.

1163
01:30:18,501 --> 01:30:21,212
But look, Doctor.
Wouldn't this nucleus of survivors...

1164
01:30:21,296 --> 01:30:26,384
be so grief-stricken
and anguished that they...

1165
01:30:26,468 --> 01:30:29,971
well, envy the dead
and not want to go on living?

1166
01:30:30,055 --> 01:30:32,891
No, sir. Excuse me.

1167
01:30:42,150 --> 01:30:46,112
When they go down into the mine,
everyone would still be alive.

1168
01:30:46,154 --> 01:30:48,239
There would be
no shocking memories...

1169
01:30:48,323 --> 01:30:52,994
and the prevailing emotion will be one
of nostalgia for those left behind...

1170
01:30:53,078 --> 01:30:55,955
combined with a spirit of...

1171
01:30:55,997 --> 01:30:58,458
bold curiosity for
the adventure ahead!

1172
01:31:15,975 --> 01:31:17,894
Doctor...

1173
01:31:20,105 --> 01:31:25,527
you mentioned the ratio
often women to each man.

1174
01:31:25,610 --> 01:31:28,738
Now, wouldn't that
necessitate the abandonment...

1175
01:31:28,822 --> 01:31:32,617
of the so-called
monogamous sexual relationship?

1176
01:31:32,659 --> 01:31:36,287
I mean, as far as men were concerned?

1177
01:31:36,371 --> 01:31:37,747
Regrettably, yes.

1178
01:31:37,831 --> 01:31:43,169
But it is a sacrifice required
for the future of the human race.

1179
01:31:43,253 --> 01:31:48,258
I hasten to add that since each man
will be required to do prodigious...

1180
01:31:50,010 --> 01:31:51,970
service along these lines...

1181
01:31:52,012 --> 01:31:55,807
the women will have to be selected
for their sexual characteristics...

1182
01:31:55,890 --> 01:31:59,644
which will have to be of
a highly stimulating nature.

1183
01:31:59,728 --> 01:32:03,565
I must confess, you have an
astonishingly good idea there, Doctor.

1184
01:32:04,733 --> 01:32:06,192
Thank you, sir.

1185
01:32:06,234 --> 01:32:09,195
We ought to look at this
from the military point of view.

1186
01:32:09,279 --> 01:32:13,199
I mean,
supposing the Ruskies...

1187
01:32:13,283 --> 01:32:16,202
stashed away some big bombs,
see, and we didn't?

1188
01:32:16,286 --> 01:32:19,205
When they come out in 1 00 years,
they could take over!

1189
01:32:19,247 --> 01:32:20,999
I agree, Mr. President.

1190
01:32:21,082 --> 01:32:24,669
They might try a sneak attack so they
could take over our mine shaft space.

1191
01:32:24,753 --> 01:32:29,382
It'd be extremely naive of us to
imagine that these new developments...

1192
01:32:29,466 --> 01:32:32,385
are gonna cause any change
in Soviet expansionist policy!

1193
01:32:32,469 --> 01:32:35,305
I mean, we must be
increasingly on the alert...

1194
01:32:35,388 --> 01:32:37,891
to prevent them from taking over
other mine shaft space...

1195
01:32:37,974 --> 01:32:39,893
in order to breed more
prodigiously than we do...

1196
01:32:39,976 --> 01:32:43,104
thus knocking us out through
superior numbers when we emerge!

1197
01:32:43,188 --> 01:32:47,275
Mr. President, we must not allow
a mine-shaft gap!

1198
01:32:47,359 --> 01:32:49,444
Sir!

1199
01:32:49,527 --> 01:32:51,780
I have a plan--

1200
01:32:53,323 --> 01:32:55,658
Mein Fuhrer...

1201
01:32:55,742 --> 01:32:58,328
I can walk!
